1
00:00:00,553 --> 00:00:02,840
(The first video meeting
after the loss to Altos)

2
00:00:07,457 --> 00:00:10,826
(Only silence fills the air.)

3
00:00:11,195 --> 00:00:14,364
I've heard something about the last match.

4
00:00:14,898 --> 00:00:17,767
A lot of players cried after it.

5
00:00:21,539 --> 00:00:22,973
But that's not where it should end.

6
00:00:22,974 --> 00:00:26,504
We should learn from
how we played last time.

7
00:00:27,283 --> 00:00:29,171
We should take more than
just tears from this.

8
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:30,979
And that's what worried me.

9
00:00:33,952 --> 00:00:34,952
This is our score sheet.

10
00:00:34,953 --> 00:00:37,621
You guys haven't seen this, have you?

11
00:00:38,757 --> 00:00:40,290
Our passes were...

12
00:00:41,259 --> 00:00:43,193
better than Altos.

13
00:00:43,629 --> 00:00:45,228
But our attack success rate was...

14
00:00:46,631 --> 00:00:47,664
too low.

15
00:00:49,134 --> 00:00:51,811
In my opinion, our setters...

16
00:00:53,204 --> 00:00:55,405
didn't play their best.

17
00:00:55,707 --> 00:00:57,408
(Setter, Lee Jin)

18
00:00:57,575 --> 00:00:59,094
(Setter, Koo Sol)

19
00:00:59,095 --> 00:01:00,829
So I wanted to ask you this.

20
00:01:01,147 --> 00:01:04,648
During training, I think the setters...

21
00:01:04,950 --> 00:01:06,751
were actually not bad.

22
00:01:07,219 --> 00:01:10,021
But once we're in a game,

23
00:01:10,022 --> 00:01:12,624
you seem to struggle,
and I was wondering why.

24
00:01:14,332 --> 00:01:15,498
I'm not sure.

25
00:01:17,064 --> 00:01:18,730
Maybe during a game,

26
00:01:18,730 --> 00:01:22,066
I try too hard to play better,

27
00:01:22,293 --> 00:01:25,996
but it's true we weren't at our best.

28
00:01:26,238 --> 00:01:27,805
Whenever I made a mistake,

29
00:01:28,941 --> 00:01:31,276
I got too caught up in it,

30
00:01:31,276 --> 00:01:33,277
and lost my confidence.

31
00:01:34,780 --> 00:01:38,950
That's neither here nor there.

32
00:01:39,284 --> 00:01:41,885
That's not really
a constructive thing to say.

33
00:01:42,253 --> 00:01:44,489
You didn't play well
because you were nervous...

34
00:01:44,490 --> 00:01:45,856
and you lost your confidence.

35
00:01:46,426 --> 00:01:49,395
We can make a million excuses if we want.

36
00:01:49,930 --> 00:01:52,198
But this was our second game.

37
00:01:52,466 --> 00:01:54,967
It wasn't our first time feeling that way.

38
00:01:55,035 --> 00:01:56,969
Was this the first time
you felt insecure in a game?

39
00:01:56,970 --> 00:01:57,937
No.

40
00:01:58,839 --> 00:02:03,309
What I'm trying to say is,
even if you're not feeling confident,

41
00:02:03,510 --> 00:02:05,911
you should've been ready for that.

42
00:02:06,313 --> 00:02:07,914
We just weren't prepared.

43
00:02:07,914 --> 00:02:08,930
(Lack of preparation)

44
00:02:08,931 --> 00:02:11,165
The fact that you weren't prepared
for that mental state means...

45
00:02:11,551 --> 00:02:15,020
you weren't fully prepared as a player
to go on the court.

46
00:02:16,123 --> 00:02:17,824
Even if you don't have confidence,

47
00:02:17,824 --> 00:02:20,025
you have to prepare for it
and think about...

48
00:02:20,293 --> 00:02:23,128
how you can overcome it and own it.

49
00:02:23,730 --> 00:02:25,931
Didn't you have that in mind
during training?

50
00:02:26,533 --> 00:02:29,335
You already know you might feel insecure,

51
00:02:29,436 --> 00:02:32,371
so you have to make sure
you don't get there in a game.

52
00:02:32,572 --> 00:02:34,206
That's up to you.

53
00:02:35,175 --> 00:02:36,742
So we should keep that in mind...

54
00:02:36,743 --> 00:02:38,177
and work on it during training.

55
00:02:39,279 --> 00:02:42,848
(Episode 4, "We don't lose twice.")

56
00:02:43,183 --> 00:02:45,753
Come on, Na Yeon!

57
00:02:45,754 --> 00:02:47,620
Go fast and low.

58
00:02:47,621 --> 00:02:49,055
Keep your focus on her!

59
00:02:49,156 --> 00:02:51,157
Follow the ball.
They're passing right here.

60
00:02:51,157 --> 00:02:53,158
Not strong enough!

61
00:02:53,159 --> 00:02:55,160
This isn't rocket science, Su Bin!

62
00:02:55,161 --> 00:02:56,161
Don't be scared!

63
00:03:00,113 --> 00:03:01,513
(Coach Kim Tae Young)

64
00:03:02,282 --> 00:03:04,350
We're taking off soon.

65
00:03:04,718 --> 00:03:06,118
It's spacious too.

66
00:03:06,953 --> 00:03:09,321
Your knees aren't touching,

67
00:03:09,322 --> 00:03:10,889
so it's definitely spacious.

68
00:03:11,825 --> 00:03:13,726
I have no idea how good Shujitsu will be.

69
00:03:14,928 --> 00:03:16,128
In the end,

70
00:03:16,596 --> 00:03:18,797
we don't have any information
about their players.

71
00:03:18,798 --> 00:03:20,699
All we saw were those kids' fierce eyes...

72
00:03:20,967 --> 00:03:23,802
and their floor-mopping skills,

73
00:03:24,204 --> 00:03:25,771
- so we need performance analysis.
- Yes.

74
00:03:26,106 --> 00:03:28,107
We're going
to the Inter-High School Championships.

75
00:03:28,509 --> 00:03:30,442
I'm a big fan of "Haikyu!!"

76
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:34,012
and their matches took place
in the Inter-High.

77
00:03:34,691 --> 00:03:36,595
It's like
the Korean National Sports Festival.

78
00:03:37,110 --> 00:03:39,511
Japanese volleyball shows...

79
00:03:39,512 --> 00:03:41,346
- exceptional technical skills.
- Yes.

80
00:03:41,347 --> 00:03:42,112
I mean it.

81
00:03:42,533 --> 00:03:44,767
That's how serious they are
about volleyball.

82
00:03:45,228 --> 00:03:48,964
Their mindset is already different
from ours.

83
00:03:49,996 --> 00:03:51,929
We've prepared lunch for you.

84
00:03:52,030 --> 00:03:52,997
Enjoy, coach.

85
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,134
I like this noodle salad.

86
00:03:57,168 --> 00:03:58,668
It's a big portion. I like it.

87
00:03:58,670 --> 00:04:00,304
(Incheon International Airport, Korea)

88
00:04:00,305 --> 00:04:01,705
(Takamatsu Airport, Japan)

89
00:04:01,706 --> 00:04:02,739
We're in Japan now.

90
00:04:03,108 --> 00:04:06,143
(Searching for a clue to victory)

91
00:04:10,048 --> 00:04:11,515
(Zip Arena Okayama)

92
00:04:11,516 --> 00:04:12,349
Is that it?

93
00:04:14,386 --> 00:04:15,353
Impressive.

94
00:04:15,353 --> 00:04:17,287
And this is a high-school tournament.

95
00:04:17,288 --> 00:04:20,524
- This is huge.
- The arena is huge too.

96
00:04:21,893 --> 00:04:23,293
This is really big.

97
00:04:23,728 --> 00:04:25,229
It's like the Olympics.

98
00:04:26,231 --> 00:04:27,198
They sell merch too.

99
00:04:32,304 --> 00:04:34,038
- Yeon Koung?
- Yeon Koung!

100
00:04:34,139 --> 00:04:35,305
It's Kim Yeon Koung.

101
00:04:35,874 --> 00:04:37,541
They all recognize you.

102
00:04:39,177 --> 00:04:40,244
Hello.

103
00:04:41,646 --> 00:04:42,613
Hello.

104
00:04:42,814 --> 00:04:43,580
Hi.

105
00:04:45,317 --> 00:04:46,317
- They all know you.
- Hi there.

106
00:04:46,317 --> 00:04:47,350
(Saying hello to everyone)

107
00:04:47,752 --> 00:04:50,987
(Even a shy photo request)

108
00:04:51,615 --> 00:04:52,582
Hello.

109
00:04:52,949 --> 00:04:54,316
- Hello.
- Hi.

110
00:04:55,562 --> 00:04:57,195
(Forming a crowd)

111
00:04:59,565 --> 00:05:02,567
(Photo requests pouring in)

112
00:05:03,589 --> 00:05:05,356
I should start charging.
I know, right?

113
00:05:05,371 --> 00:05:06,204
For money.

114
00:05:06,572 --> 00:05:08,173
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

115
00:05:08,174 --> 00:05:09,441
Thank you.

116
00:05:09,442 --> 00:05:11,276
How do they know
how to say that in Korean?

117
00:05:11,624 --> 00:05:12,857
It's so crowded.

118
00:05:12,865 --> 00:05:14,666
(Pushing their way
through the packed crowd)

119
00:05:18,471 --> 00:05:19,571
Look at this.

120
00:05:19,572 --> 00:05:20,705
(Admiring)

121
00:05:20,706 --> 00:05:23,474
This is today's match lineup.

122
00:05:23,476 --> 00:05:24,743
Fascinating.

123
00:05:25,478 --> 00:05:27,679
When I heard that over 50 schools...

124
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:30,282
come to play in the tournament,

125
00:05:30,483 --> 00:05:32,350
I was quite surprised.

126
00:05:37,252 --> 00:05:39,286
(Who are these two people
next to Coach Yeon Koung?)

127
00:05:39,407 --> 00:05:41,710
(Libero, Inoue Kotoe)

128
00:05:42,074 --> 00:05:44,075
(Interpreter, Shin Dong Ju)

129
00:05:44,364 --> 00:05:47,103
(Her former colleagues came to
help Yeon Koung at her first Inter-High.)

130
00:05:50,934 --> 00:05:54,637
(The cheering squad
bursting with energy and presence.)

131
00:05:55,698 --> 00:05:57,934
Who are those people cheering?

132
00:05:58,167 --> 00:05:59,135
Mostly parents.

133
00:05:59,277 --> 00:06:02,546
Parents and players who aren't playing.

134
00:06:04,497 --> 00:06:06,431
Those parents' cheering is...

135
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:08,868
knife-synchronized.

136
00:06:09,736 --> 00:06:11,470
(Perfect unison)

137
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:13,647
(Plus intensity)

138
00:06:13,648 --> 00:06:15,348
My jaw's dropping.

139
00:06:17,444 --> 00:06:20,379
They're freaking me out a bit.
Look at them.

140
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:23,315
(It's like an army choreography.)

141
00:06:24,377 --> 00:06:28,947
(This is another highlight
of the Inter-High School Championships.)

142
00:06:29,934 --> 00:06:33,308
You can see
that all the players have short hair.

143
00:06:33,637 --> 00:06:35,297
Is there a reason?

144
00:06:35,791 --> 00:06:39,001
Now, more teams are
allowing their players to have long hair,

145
00:06:39,269 --> 00:06:42,745
but back then, we were required
to have short hair.

146
00:06:44,504 --> 00:06:46,345
We were also the same in Korea.

147
00:06:47,813 --> 00:06:49,069
(There are no hairstyle regulations
in Korea now.)

148
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:50,643
It has changed a lot,

149
00:06:50,883 --> 00:06:52,496
but they still have the regulations.

150
00:06:53,096 --> 00:06:55,308
We'll be facing...

151
00:06:55,309 --> 00:06:56,483
Shujitsu High School.

152
00:06:56,939 --> 00:07:00,503
I wonder how good they are.

153
00:07:01,404 --> 00:07:02,752
They're unbelievable.

154
00:07:02,753 --> 00:07:04,340
She said they were unbelievable.

155
00:07:04,707 --> 00:07:05,778
- "Unbelievable?"
- Yes.

156
00:07:06,375 --> 00:07:08,167
Because they're really good,
they have no matches today.

157
00:07:08,168 --> 00:07:12,514
They skipped preliminary matches,
so their matches start tomorrow.

158
00:07:13,101 --> 00:07:16,171
(Out of over 4,000 high schools in Japan,)

159
00:07:16,425 --> 00:07:19,117
(Shujitsu High is one of the best.)

160
00:07:19,588 --> 00:07:21,890
(But the superstar is...)

161
00:07:23,051 --> 00:07:25,420
(only feeling refreshed.)

162
00:07:26,755 --> 00:07:29,091
(The moisture barrier
that's as solid as Shujitsu High.)

163
00:07:30,493 --> 00:07:33,663
(Stop there, Shujitsu!)

164
00:07:35,288 --> 00:07:38,417
(The analysis of Shujitsu High's strength
begins.)

165
00:07:40,045 --> 00:07:42,045
They look like they're strong.

166
00:07:42,391 --> 00:07:43,391
She must be their coach.

167
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:46,675
(Nishihata Miki,
the coach of Shujitsu High School)

168
00:07:46,695 --> 00:07:48,776
The coach looks very charismatic.

169
00:07:49,869 --> 00:07:52,781
(Overwhelming presence)

170
00:07:54,507 --> 00:07:56,188
Coach Kim, they're the supporters
of Shujitsu High.

171
00:07:56,407 --> 00:07:57,856
They're so fierce.

172
00:07:57,857 --> 00:08:00,358
(Even their cheering is fierce.)

173
00:08:01,514 --> 00:08:05,284
(They are pretty intimidating!)

174
00:08:05,806 --> 00:08:08,959
I realized they were stronger
than I'd thought.

175
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:10,206
(Pensive)

176
00:08:10,716 --> 00:08:12,963
Of course, it won't be an easy game,

177
00:08:13,489 --> 00:08:16,419
but I've also come up with my own plan.

178
00:08:16,472 --> 00:08:19,745
I believe we stand a chance.

179
00:08:20,352 --> 00:08:23,151
So, we are going to win.

180
00:08:26,822 --> 00:08:30,159
(While the players are training)

181
00:08:30,826 --> 00:08:32,094
(Go for it!)

182
00:08:32,454 --> 00:08:33,753
(She came to the gym right away.)

183
00:08:33,766 --> 00:08:35,785
- Hi.
- Hello.

184
00:08:37,286 --> 00:08:39,096
I just got back from Japan,

185
00:08:39,516 --> 00:08:42,049
so I'm suffering from jet lag.

186
00:08:42,050 --> 00:08:43,980
(She's right back to work.)

187
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:45,840
We have no choice.

188
00:08:46,256 --> 00:08:51,417
Since we must beat the Japanese team,

189
00:08:51,926 --> 00:08:54,888
I went straight to the gym
from the airport.

190
00:08:55,594 --> 00:08:58,361
How many days a week
are you spending on this show?

191
00:08:59,359 --> 00:09:02,365
I didn't take a day off this week.

192
00:09:03,206 --> 00:09:07,109
And I don't think I'll have any free days
next week either.

193
00:09:07,370 --> 00:09:09,272
The thought of the busy schedule...

194
00:09:09,682 --> 00:09:11,382
makes me want to cry.

195
00:09:12,002 --> 00:09:14,734
I'd like to ask you to stop
talking about it.

196
00:09:15,181 --> 00:09:17,693
(When was the last time
I really had a proper rest?)

197
00:09:17,846 --> 00:09:19,699
You're even working harder
than when you were a player.

198
00:09:20,465 --> 00:09:21,345
Gosh!

199
00:09:22,485 --> 00:09:25,531
I got fooled by MBC.

200
00:09:25,885 --> 00:09:27,885
The producer tricked me.

201
00:09:27,892 --> 00:09:29,459
He's a con artist.

202
00:09:30,332 --> 00:09:32,472
Look. I've lost my voice...

203
00:09:32,495 --> 00:09:34,641
as well as my private life.

204
00:09:36,188 --> 00:09:41,330
I'm so worried that my voice might
sound really terrible on TV.

205
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:43,299
Why are all the interviews so long?

206
00:09:43,366 --> 00:09:46,085
Why do you even ask me so many questions
when you're editing most of them out?

207
00:09:46,186 --> 00:09:47,296
(Checking the time)

208
00:09:47,309 --> 00:09:49,849
It's already 11 p.m.!

209
00:09:52,582 --> 00:09:55,875
You're insane!
We have a plan at six in the morning!

210
00:09:57,682 --> 00:10:01,725
You've done it up to this point, right?
We have a game against a Japanese team.

211
00:10:02,165 --> 00:10:03,698
I saw them, and they were good.

212
00:10:04,198 --> 00:10:07,752
They hardly miss a ball...

213
00:10:07,849 --> 00:10:10,969
once it's on the court.

214
00:10:11,245 --> 00:10:16,037
I've been thinking
about how to break their defense.

215
00:10:16,569 --> 00:10:18,569
We should go
with a team-wide all-out attack.

216
00:10:19,142 --> 00:10:20,482
A full-on team attack.

217
00:10:20,655 --> 00:10:23,588
Their defense is quite tight,

218
00:10:23,735 --> 00:10:26,068
so to break it and score points,

219
00:10:26,375 --> 00:10:30,918
I think focusing on an all-out attack is
important.

220
00:10:31,062 --> 00:10:33,276
From the serve and blocking to the attack.

221
00:10:33,483 --> 00:10:36,490
Blocking is regarded as defense,

222
00:10:36,803 --> 00:10:39,329
but it's another form of attack.

223
00:10:39,522 --> 00:10:41,522
This strategy will play the key role
in our victory.

224
00:10:41,769 --> 00:10:45,879
Our chances to score a point
against Shujitsu High come...

225
00:10:45,968 --> 00:10:48,208
when they are blocking.

226
00:10:49,617 --> 00:10:51,686
(While the ball comes
over to their court,)

227
00:10:51,719 --> 00:10:53,420
The middle blocker's movement is dull.

228
00:10:53,444 --> 00:10:55,081
(the middle blocker finds it hard
to follow the ball.)

229
00:10:55,100 --> 00:10:58,025
That's where we'll get attacking chances.

230
00:10:58,226 --> 00:11:02,165
If the setters set the ball,
they'll have to perform a solo block.

231
00:11:02,705 --> 00:11:05,778
Because there's only one blocker,

232
00:11:06,459 --> 00:11:08,265
we have a better chance of scoring.

233
00:11:09,024 --> 00:11:12,706
If the setters do a little better job...

234
00:11:12,904 --> 00:11:16,003
You don't have to excel,
but do just a bit better job.

235
00:11:16,090 --> 00:11:18,445
Then, whenever the opposing team
performs a solo attack,

236
00:11:18,823 --> 00:11:23,046
we'll keep having a chance
to spike for a point.

237
00:11:25,292 --> 00:11:27,788
The setter will see
how the middle blocker moves...

238
00:11:30,070 --> 00:11:31,859
and set the ball,

239
00:11:32,057 --> 00:11:35,036
which is the basic skill.
Then, we will be able...

240
00:11:35,049 --> 00:11:37,829
to have them make a solo block, right?

241
00:11:38,682 --> 00:11:42,058
In that situation,
we have a better chanceof scoring.

242
00:11:43,125 --> 00:11:46,240
So, when that happens,
all of you will focus on attacking.

243
00:11:46,241 --> 00:11:48,211
(Until their defense breaks down,
they'll focus on attacking.)

244
00:11:48,212 --> 00:11:52,441
Today, we will practice how to attack
and how to score.

245
00:11:52,908 --> 00:11:54,649
Watch the opponent's moment!

246
00:11:54,968 --> 00:11:57,407
(A quick glance)

247
00:11:58,180 --> 00:12:00,060
Watch how she reacts! Lift it!

248
00:12:00,421 --> 00:12:01,866
(There's only one blocker.)

249
00:12:01,892 --> 00:12:04,059
That's it! Good.

250
00:12:04,291 --> 00:12:07,361
- Sol, Good. Keep watching the opponent.
- Okay.

251
00:12:12,633 --> 00:12:14,692
(Jin, the setter)

252
00:12:14,711 --> 00:12:17,938
Please watch her movement first.
I'm begging you.

253
00:12:18,162 --> 00:12:19,162
Watch her and play, please.

254
00:12:20,641 --> 00:12:22,309
Hit it!

255
00:12:23,481 --> 00:12:24,481
Hit it!

256
00:12:25,401 --> 00:12:27,937
Na Yeon, Myoung Hwa stepped in first.

257
00:12:28,150 --> 00:12:29,635
Then, you should've gone
to the opposite side.

258
00:12:30,204 --> 00:12:31,424
Make sure to watch her.

259
00:12:34,936 --> 00:12:36,576
Sol, are you watching the middle blocker?

260
00:12:37,036 --> 00:12:38,060
You followed it well.

261
00:12:38,681 --> 00:12:40,662
Keep watching.

262
00:12:41,488 --> 00:12:42,982
How frustrating.

263
00:12:46,234 --> 00:12:47,234
Come here.

264
00:12:47,787 --> 00:12:49,787
How do you think the training is going?

265
00:12:51,186 --> 00:12:53,690
- Are we practicing a hard skill now?
- No.

266
00:12:54,733 --> 00:12:56,996
There is a reason
our attack success rate is low.

267
00:12:57,366 --> 00:12:58,371
Why do you think that is?

268
00:12:59,226 --> 00:13:01,932
You are not passing a proper ball.
How can they hit it, then?

269
00:13:02,999 --> 00:13:06,439
If you do not have the basics down,
how are you going to score?

270
00:13:07,442 --> 00:13:11,111
It is a set routine,
so why is it getting so messy and chaotic?

271
00:13:12,067 --> 00:13:13,494
If we lose three more games,
it is all over.

272
00:13:14,574 --> 00:13:15,994
It's all over, then.

273
00:13:16,547 --> 00:13:19,418
This is not a joke.
But if you keep playing like this,

274
00:13:19,703 --> 00:13:21,129
it will end quickly.

275
00:13:21,130 --> 00:13:24,323
Even when you are relaxing,
don't just fool around, but keep thinking.

276
00:13:24,918 --> 00:13:25,918
Do you understand?

277
00:13:26,793 --> 00:13:30,687
(Keep going until you succeed.)

278
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:32,881
(Peeping)

279
00:13:33,170 --> 00:13:36,485
Watch the middle blocker.

280
00:13:36,998 --> 00:13:39,129
Do it while visualizing.

281
00:13:39,352 --> 00:13:42,957
Just keep watching the middle blocker.

282
00:13:42,958 --> 00:13:45,633
Sol, you darn girl!

283
00:13:47,651 --> 00:13:50,974
If your defense is this poor,
I'll leave you at Shujitsu High behind.

284
00:13:51,086 --> 00:13:52,245
Watch Myoung Hwa.

285
00:13:52,393 --> 00:13:54,392
Watch Myoung Hwa. Good!

286
00:13:54,393 --> 00:13:56,045
(Getting better at reading
the middle blocker's positioning)

287
00:13:56,046 --> 00:13:58,728
That's right. Great.

288
00:13:58,908 --> 00:14:02,121
Suzuki High players are quite strong.
They just smash the ball.

289
00:14:02,488 --> 00:14:04,804
- Is it Suzuki? Oh, Shujitsu.
- Shujitsu.

290
00:14:04,805 --> 00:14:06,553
"Suzuki" a is a way different thing.

291
00:14:07,637 --> 00:14:09,694
(Once the setter understands the plan,)

292
00:14:11,074 --> 00:14:13,074
(the hitters are on fire too.)

293
00:14:13,098 --> 00:14:14,865
Hitters, let's go and beat Shujitsu!

294
00:14:20,249 --> 00:14:22,351
(Engaging their entire bodies,)

295
00:14:22,730 --> 00:14:25,199
(they're reinforcing their muscles.)

296
00:14:25,747 --> 00:14:27,923
I think they're all the same flavor.

297
00:14:28,293 --> 00:14:29,293
What are these?

298
00:14:31,099 --> 00:14:34,269
(The rookie coach's presents
for the players)

299
00:14:34,622 --> 00:14:37,806
- Is that enzyme juice?
- That's right.

300
00:14:38,442 --> 00:14:39,641
It's all the rage right now.

301
00:14:40,206 --> 00:14:41,376
It's really simple.

302
00:14:41,826 --> 00:14:43,889
Since it's hard
to eat a lot of vegetables,

303
00:14:43,949 --> 00:14:46,242
we need to juice them like this
and drink them.

304
00:14:46,409 --> 00:14:47,549
I also drink it all the time.

305
00:14:48,479 --> 00:14:51,006
- This tastes healthy.
- I can taste the tomato too.

306
00:14:51,179 --> 00:14:53,666
- Doesn't it taste like basil?
- It does.

307
00:14:53,899 --> 00:14:55,090
We must crush them, okay?

308
00:14:55,559 --> 00:14:57,641
- That's the mindset you should have.
- Yes, ma'am.

309
00:14:57,642 --> 00:15:00,876
You're probably planning to shop there.

310
00:15:03,065 --> 00:15:04,065
But if you lose,

311
00:15:04,065 --> 00:15:06,432
don't you dare try to leave your dorm.

312
00:15:06,432 --> 00:15:07,699
This is an order.

313
00:15:08,064 --> 00:15:09,498
Got it? It's an order.

314
00:15:12,165 --> 00:15:14,457
It will be so embarrassing
to go home if we lose to Japan.

315
00:15:14,458 --> 00:15:15,658
(To the enemies' territory)

316
00:15:17,132 --> 00:15:19,632
We might have to take a boat or swim.

317
00:15:21,865 --> 00:15:25,599
(The match day, Japan)

318
00:15:26,418 --> 00:15:30,346
(Gymnasium 3, Shujitsu High School)

319
00:15:32,457 --> 00:15:34,333
(Together with the local staff,)

320
00:15:34,334 --> 00:15:36,266
(The stadium announcer)

321
00:15:39,096 --> 00:15:43,974
(they even brought
in the entire broadcast truck.)

322
00:15:45,815 --> 00:15:48,615
(And there are six referees?)

323
00:15:48,970 --> 00:15:50,570
There won't be a video review today.

324
00:15:50,570 --> 00:15:51,737
- No video review?
- Nope.

325
00:15:52,304 --> 00:15:53,737
If there's no video review...

326
00:15:54,004 --> 00:15:57,404
I'd better make a move then!

327
00:15:57,770 --> 00:15:59,804
We should take some action
on the game today.

328
00:15:59,804 --> 00:16:01,777
(Today's match doesn't have
a video review.)

329
00:16:01,870 --> 00:16:04,370
Our third match is
an international competition.

330
00:16:04,370 --> 00:16:06,504
Moreover, it's the Korea-Japan match.

331
00:16:07,470 --> 00:16:09,237
Wonder Dogs' opposing team is...

332
00:16:09,237 --> 00:16:12,337
Shujitsu High School,
the strongest high school team in Japan.

333
00:16:12,837 --> 00:16:15,370
Last year, they won
the National High School Championship.

334
00:16:15,770 --> 00:16:17,804
They also won
the Inter-High Championship thrice...

335
00:16:18,170 --> 00:16:20,604
and five times
in the Spring High School Tournament.

336
00:16:20,604 --> 00:16:22,837
You can say they're the top team
in high school volleyball.

337
00:16:24,137 --> 00:16:26,537
That's Senba Kokoro,
who won the Best Libero Award...

338
00:16:26,537 --> 00:16:28,570
at the World Championship.

339
00:16:32,536 --> 00:16:36,432
(Players of Shujitsu High School give
all they've got even before the match.)

340
00:16:39,637 --> 00:16:41,570
Their steps are no joke.

341
00:16:42,537 --> 00:16:44,170
They're already warmed up.

342
00:16:45,804 --> 00:16:48,837
(Peeking)

343
00:16:48,837 --> 00:16:52,137
More than a hundred are here
as their cheering squad.

344
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:55,570
Japan has its own cheering style.

345
00:16:55,904 --> 00:16:58,370
Wonder Dogs must overcome
the cheering focused on their opponents.

346
00:16:58,370 --> 00:16:59,570
Okay.

347
00:16:59,770 --> 00:17:01,704
Even for the place here,

348
00:17:01,704 --> 00:17:04,604
the floor is made of wood,
which isn't common in Korea.

349
00:17:04,604 --> 00:17:05,937
- That's right.
- A wooden floor.

350
00:17:10,870 --> 00:17:13,104
Unlike our court,

351
00:17:13,104 --> 00:17:15,037
their floor is made of wood.

352
00:17:15,070 --> 00:17:18,470
So when players try to dig,
receive, or move around,

353
00:17:18,470 --> 00:17:20,704
they might feel a little different.

354
00:17:21,037 --> 00:17:24,737
But once the game starts,
it will all be excuses.

355
00:17:24,737 --> 00:17:28,437
Players must play the game
in a very different environment.

356
00:17:28,437 --> 00:17:30,037
(They must compete with skills alone.)

357
00:17:30,037 --> 00:17:35,337
We now ask both teams to stand
facing each other for the greeting.

358
00:17:36,070 --> 00:17:40,070
Korean players used to have
confidence and composure.

359
00:17:40,104 --> 00:17:42,337
I don't think they do anymore.

360
00:17:42,570 --> 00:17:44,870
This is a do-or-die battle.

361
00:17:45,704 --> 00:17:49,937
With no excuse or reason,
I believe we should always...

362
00:17:50,470 --> 00:17:53,104
win the match against Japan,
no matter what.

363
00:17:59,637 --> 00:18:00,737
Let's have a good game.

364
00:18:03,070 --> 00:18:05,670
Here's Wonder Dogs' lineup,
which Coach Kim carefully decided.

365
00:18:05,904 --> 00:18:07,570
First, we have Lee Na Yeon as the setter.

366
00:18:07,570 --> 00:18:09,104
Pyo Seung Ju as the outside hitter.

367
00:18:09,104 --> 00:18:10,570
Moon Myoung Hwa, the middle blocker.

368
00:18:10,570 --> 00:18:12,170
Yoon Young In, the opposite hitter.

369
00:18:12,170 --> 00:18:13,904
Back Chae Rim, the outside hitter.

370
00:18:13,904 --> 00:18:15,204
Kim Hyeon Jeong, the middle blocker.

371
00:18:15,204 --> 00:18:16,670
And Koo Hye In is the libero.

372
00:18:16,670 --> 00:18:20,537
Let's move on to the lineup
of Shujitsu High School against them.

373
00:18:20,537 --> 00:18:22,037
Kato Uta is the setter.

374
00:18:22,037 --> 00:18:24,070
Yoshimoto Kanade, the outside hitter.

375
00:18:24,070 --> 00:18:26,004
Ishida Megumi, the middle blocker.

376
00:18:26,004 --> 00:18:28,237
Ushida Otoha, the opposite hitter.

377
00:18:28,237 --> 00:18:30,570
Mitsumori Airi, the outside hitter.

378
00:18:30,570 --> 00:18:32,537
Hiruma Miharu, the middle blocker.

379
00:18:32,537 --> 00:18:34,537
And Senba Kokoro is the libero.

380
00:18:35,404 --> 00:18:37,337
Think of where you'll attack first.

381
00:18:37,504 --> 00:18:39,604
Don't mind them defending
with a single block.

382
00:18:39,937 --> 00:18:41,204
- Understood?
- Yes, Coach.

383
00:18:41,837 --> 00:18:43,504
When our setters check
on their middle blocker...

384
00:18:43,504 --> 00:18:47,104
and play tricks with their tosses,
they will definitely use a single block.

385
00:18:47,470 --> 00:18:48,537
Let's go.

386
00:18:48,537 --> 00:18:50,570
- Pilseung!
- Wonder Dogs!

387
00:18:51,237 --> 00:18:54,004
Don't ever give up.

388
00:18:54,004 --> 00:18:56,204
- Yes, Coach!
- Let's all be strong and go for it.

389
00:18:56,656 --> 00:18:58,556
(Let's go, Shujitsu!)

390
00:19:00,892 --> 00:19:02,159
A battle between Wonder Dogs...

391
00:19:02,992 --> 00:19:04,959
and Shujitsu High School.

392
00:19:05,739 --> 00:19:08,172
Wonder Dogs'
first international competition.

393
00:19:09,692 --> 00:19:13,426
Their match begins with Kato Uta's serve.

394
00:19:14,726 --> 00:19:15,726
The first set starts!

395
00:19:18,392 --> 00:19:21,126
(A shaky reception?)

396
00:19:21,526 --> 00:19:23,259
Young In!

397
00:19:23,259 --> 00:19:24,892
(Seung Ju rushes to toss.)

398
00:19:25,226 --> 00:19:26,459
Young In sent the ball over the net.

399
00:19:26,692 --> 00:19:29,359
(Shujitsu High School's chance to attack)

400
00:19:29,586 --> 00:19:30,710
Let's go!

401
00:19:30,750 --> 00:19:32,150
(Ushida's spike)

402
00:19:32,221 --> 00:19:33,621
A spike to the right!

403
00:19:34,426 --> 00:19:35,459
It hits the ground.

404
00:19:36,812 --> 00:19:39,112
(They end up losing a point.)

405
00:19:39,751 --> 00:19:44,118
(The opposing team gets
their first point easily.)

406
00:19:48,451 --> 00:19:52,759
(Setters were supposed to be
the key part of their strategy.)

407
00:19:53,718 --> 00:19:57,884
(But Na Yeon couldn't even touch the ball
due to their poor reception.)

408
00:19:58,618 --> 00:19:59,884
My mistake!

409
00:19:59,884 --> 00:20:02,051
- It's okay.
- Receive it first.

410
00:20:02,384 --> 00:20:04,251
Chae Rim, lower your body.
It's not stable.

411
00:20:04,251 --> 00:20:06,251
Watch out for the short serve.

412
00:20:07,584 --> 00:20:08,784
It's one to zero.

413
00:20:08,784 --> 00:20:10,362
(First set, Shujitsu High School 1:
Wonder Dogs 0)

414
00:20:12,551 --> 00:20:14,318
Mine! Na Yeon!

415
00:20:15,251 --> 00:20:16,284
(Nice catch.)

416
00:20:16,551 --> 00:20:17,584
Na Yeon!

417
00:20:19,718 --> 00:20:20,951
Na Yeon launches a back toss.

418
00:20:20,951 --> 00:20:22,184
Hit it!

419
00:20:24,384 --> 00:20:27,551
(But the toss is high?)

420
00:20:29,318 --> 00:20:30,718
It was a bit high.

421
00:20:30,718 --> 00:20:32,818
(The ball went in a weak spike.)

422
00:20:34,757 --> 00:20:36,757
(Their opposing team gets
to attack again.)

423
00:20:39,684 --> 00:20:41,584
A spike to the middle!

424
00:20:43,384 --> 00:20:46,318
(Ishida's mind-blowing power)

425
00:20:46,984 --> 00:20:49,884
(They quickly score in a row.)

426
00:20:49,884 --> 00:20:52,284
Na Yeon, your toss is too high.

427
00:20:53,384 --> 00:20:54,584
Come on!

428
00:20:54,584 --> 00:20:56,284
(It's okay. Let's do this!)

429
00:20:56,784 --> 00:20:57,818
It's two to zero.

430
00:20:57,818 --> 00:20:59,251
(Shujitsu High School 2: Wonder Dogs 0)

431
00:21:01,151 --> 00:21:02,351
Mine! Na Yeon!

432
00:21:02,351 --> 00:21:03,384
(It's a nice reception.)

433
00:21:04,118 --> 00:21:05,318
Na Yeon sends it up again.

434
00:21:07,984 --> 00:21:09,418
The toss is too low this time!

435
00:21:09,418 --> 00:21:10,918
(It falls down fast?)

436
00:21:12,384 --> 00:21:13,618
(Hitting and blocking softly)

437
00:21:17,751 --> 00:21:20,451
(They lose another point.)

438
00:21:20,451 --> 00:21:21,518
Hey!

439
00:21:23,651 --> 00:21:27,151
They must be tossing far first...

440
00:21:27,151 --> 00:21:33,384
to make the middle blocker move a lot.

441
00:21:34,284 --> 00:21:35,418
Hey!

442
00:21:35,418 --> 00:21:38,384
Guys, what should we do at the start?

443
00:21:38,484 --> 00:21:40,318
Concentrate!

444
00:21:42,584 --> 00:21:43,951
(But...)

445
00:21:43,951 --> 00:21:44,951
Mine!

446
00:21:45,784 --> 00:21:46,784
Mine!

447
00:21:46,784 --> 00:21:48,418
(Tumbling)

448
00:21:51,918 --> 00:21:54,084
(Yoshimoto's spike)

449
00:21:55,851 --> 00:21:57,984
(Shujitsu High School 4: Wonder Dogs 0)

450
00:21:59,518 --> 00:22:00,851
(Number 3, Ishida Megumi)

451
00:22:00,851 --> 00:22:02,084
A spike to the middle!

452
00:22:02,084 --> 00:22:04,418
(Shujitsu High School 5: Wonder Dogs 0)

453
00:22:05,684 --> 00:22:07,751
Shoot!

454
00:22:09,018 --> 00:22:13,284
(Shujitsu High School's relentless attacks
shake the Wonder Dogs.)

455
00:22:13,951 --> 00:22:16,818
- At this rate...
- They can't lose more points.

456
00:22:16,818 --> 00:22:17,951
It's zero to five.

457
00:22:17,951 --> 00:22:22,051
The game is turning out
like the match against the Altos.

458
00:22:25,951 --> 00:22:28,218
Coach Kim immediately requests
the timeout.

459
00:22:28,218 --> 00:22:30,484
(Wonder Dogs' timeout)

460
00:22:31,618 --> 00:22:33,751
What are you doing?

461
00:22:33,751 --> 00:22:36,251
What are you all doing from the start?

462
00:22:36,584 --> 00:22:38,484
- Your toss was too high at first.
- Yes, Coach.

463
00:22:38,484 --> 00:22:40,118
- And then it got too low.
- Understood.

464
00:22:40,118 --> 00:22:42,751
Bend your knees.
Don't receive the ball too high.

465
00:22:42,751 --> 00:22:44,184
(Their tactics weren't used at all
in the beginning.)

466
00:22:44,184 --> 00:22:45,618
I'll hit it, no matter what.

467
00:22:45,618 --> 00:22:47,118
It's not just about attacks.

468
00:22:47,118 --> 00:22:49,784
Think of coverage too.
It leads to points.

469
00:22:49,784 --> 00:22:50,951
We must do it.

470
00:22:51,918 --> 00:22:52,951
(Let's do our thing!)

471
00:22:52,951 --> 00:22:55,351
Focus when you play.

472
00:22:55,618 --> 00:22:57,518
We won't get another chance after this.

473
00:22:57,518 --> 00:22:59,218
- Just one point!
- Come on!

474
00:23:00,584 --> 00:23:05,784
(Their opponents are stronger
than they expected.)

475
00:23:06,384 --> 00:23:09,218
(We need to turn the tables...)

476
00:23:09,218 --> 00:23:11,551
(with our own style.)

477
00:23:15,184 --> 00:23:16,384
It's okay!

478
00:23:16,918 --> 00:23:19,484
It's fine, so concentrate.
We can do this step by step.

479
00:23:20,318 --> 00:23:23,184
(Shujitsu High School 5: Wonder Dogs 0)

480
00:23:25,684 --> 00:23:26,684
Mine!

481
00:23:26,684 --> 00:23:29,518
(She received it well.)

482
00:23:29,684 --> 00:23:31,284
(Next is...)

483
00:23:31,418 --> 00:23:33,351
(Na Yeon's toss.)

484
00:23:33,384 --> 00:23:34,451
(Glancing)

485
00:23:34,851 --> 00:23:35,851
(Glancing)

486
00:23:36,084 --> 00:23:37,951
(Checked the middle blocker!)

487
00:23:39,484 --> 00:23:41,218
(She tossed the ball away
from their middle blocker.)

488
00:23:41,951 --> 00:23:43,918
(They fell for the trick!)

489
00:23:44,384 --> 00:23:46,184
(The middle blocker is left alone
as they have planned.)

490
00:23:46,351 --> 00:23:48,818
Whatever happens, we must do it.

491
00:23:53,784 --> 00:23:55,718
(A touch out by the blocker)

492
00:23:56,384 --> 00:23:59,351
(They finally get their first point!)

493
00:24:01,184 --> 00:24:02,451
Nice!

494
00:24:02,451 --> 00:24:05,251
- It's okay.
- Guys, don't be flustered.

495
00:24:05,251 --> 00:24:08,051
Keep checking who the hitter is
in front of you.

496
00:24:08,051 --> 00:24:09,051
Okay.

497
00:24:09,051 --> 00:24:10,851
Relax. It's fine.

498
00:24:12,484 --> 00:24:14,518
(Seung Ju, serve!)

499
00:24:16,384 --> 00:24:18,718
(Roger that.)

500
00:24:18,784 --> 00:24:20,718
We can aim the serves
between the defenders.

501
00:24:20,718 --> 00:24:22,151
You know we watched their match, right?

502
00:24:22,518 --> 00:24:28,584
They often used two players
to receive the ball.

503
00:24:28,918 --> 00:24:31,284
So, where should be our target area?

504
00:24:31,551 --> 00:24:35,218
You should aim for areas
near both their sidelines.

505
00:24:36,812 --> 00:24:38,551
(Pyo Seung Ju, the captain, serves.)

506
00:24:38,551 --> 00:24:39,684
It's one to five.

507
00:24:39,951 --> 00:24:41,684
Serve!

508
00:24:41,684 --> 00:24:42,752
The ball is over there!

509
00:24:45,777 --> 00:24:48,344
(Will they attack down the middle
right away?)

510
00:24:49,192 --> 00:24:50,727
Come!

511
00:24:58,504 --> 00:25:01,877
- A spike down the middle! Yes!
- That's right. Nice block.

512
00:25:05,534 --> 00:25:07,655
- There you go! Myoung Hwa of the day!
- Myoung Hwa of the day.

513
00:25:07,656 --> 00:25:09,274
That was earlier than expected.

514
00:25:09,434 --> 00:25:12,718
Coach Kim wanted this type of play...

515
00:25:12,719 --> 00:25:15,968
and placed two tall middle blockers
in the center...

516
00:25:15,969 --> 00:25:17,557
- of the starting lineup.
- Yes.

517
00:25:18,081 --> 00:25:21,305
(Shujitsu High often attacks
down the middle.)

518
00:25:21,739 --> 00:25:23,801
(So, we've prepared something
just for you.)

519
00:25:24,083 --> 00:25:26,752
(The wall of three)

520
00:25:32,500 --> 00:25:33,740
Good job.

521
00:25:34,246 --> 00:25:35,246
Nice serve.

522
00:25:35,392 --> 00:25:37,376
Myoung Hwa, well done.

523
00:25:42,621 --> 00:25:44,990
We can still do it.

524
00:25:45,444 --> 00:25:49,682
(The momentum has shifted in an instant.)

525
00:25:51,005 --> 00:25:54,509
(Keep this momentum going!)

526
00:25:58,012 --> 00:26:00,481
(Another on-point serve)

527
00:26:00,815 --> 00:26:01,916
(But instantly)

528
00:26:02,083 --> 00:26:03,184
(A powerful spike to the left)

529
00:26:05,253 --> 00:26:06,988
(Did it just pass by?)

530
00:26:07,322 --> 00:26:10,525
(Did they fail to defend?)

531
00:26:14,381 --> 00:26:15,963
- That's right.
- She received it on defense.

532
00:26:17,267 --> 00:26:19,816
Where is the ball going?
She's rushing for it. A strong spike!

533
00:26:21,869 --> 00:26:24,071
(Did she manage to do a single block?)

534
00:26:26,474 --> 00:26:27,508
(Don't you dare.)

535
00:26:28,376 --> 00:26:29,911
(The captain, Kokoro,
plays an impenetrable defense.)

536
00:26:30,078 --> 00:26:31,546
- Now, go!
- Behind you!

537
00:26:33,982 --> 00:26:36,050
- Nice dig.
- Now, they can do it. It's connected.

538
00:26:36,368 --> 00:26:39,054
Don't rush. A high ball.
She spikes it down.

539
00:26:41,163 --> 00:26:42,163
A dink from the right side.

540
00:26:43,696 --> 00:26:45,242
- Nice defense.
- She saved it.

541
00:26:45,835 --> 00:26:47,194
Hey, do the next move!

542
00:26:48,234 --> 00:26:49,651
(Chae Rim is ready.)

543
00:26:50,421 --> 00:26:51,854
Hey, come here!

544
00:26:56,613 --> 00:26:59,253
A spike! It lands at the left!

545
00:27:03,459 --> 00:27:05,680
Good job.

546
00:27:06,306 --> 00:27:07,306
Nice job.

547
00:27:08,638 --> 00:27:10,518
Well done. Take your time.

548
00:27:10,872 --> 00:27:13,858
They fell behind by 5 points at the start
but came back with 3 consecutive points.

549
00:27:13,859 --> 00:27:15,067
(Now they are chasing.)

550
00:27:16,325 --> 00:27:18,251
(Seung Ju's third serve)

551
00:27:21,856 --> 00:27:24,465
- That's right.
- Their receive is getting unstable.

552
00:27:25,466 --> 00:27:27,735
(Will it be out like this?)

553
00:27:42,860 --> 00:27:44,100
Kokoro's diving dig!

554
00:27:47,994 --> 00:27:49,096
Chae Rim!

555
00:27:49,097 --> 00:27:50,625
Watch out for a chance!
Don't take your eyes off until the end!

556
00:27:51,225 --> 00:27:52,769
(Utilizing the receive)

557
00:27:53,152 --> 00:27:54,905
- There's no one.
- It's an unexpected attack.

558
00:27:57,434 --> 00:27:58,701
She receives it again.

559
00:28:05,314 --> 00:28:06,820
And she saves it once again.

560
00:28:09,233 --> 00:28:12,839
- Now, she receives it. A calm back toss.
- She received it.

561
00:28:13,519 --> 00:28:14,725
Young In, hit it!

562
00:28:24,757 --> 00:28:28,330
- A spike! It works!
- That was nice.

563
00:28:29,273 --> 00:28:31,830
(Young In's powerful spike)

564
00:28:31,831 --> 00:28:32,977
Hey, nice toss.

565
00:28:34,745 --> 00:28:36,777
(Smiling widely)

566
00:28:36,817 --> 00:28:38,649
Now, there's just a one-point difference
with 4 to 5.

567
00:28:39,803 --> 00:28:42,319
Young In, I won't toss it further
than your chin.

568
00:28:43,042 --> 00:28:44,921
Young In, really nicely done.
Take your breath.

569
00:28:45,656 --> 00:28:47,825
- We're almost there!
- In 1, 2, 3!

570
00:28:48,148 --> 00:28:49,742
Nice serve!

571
00:28:51,517 --> 00:28:53,452
(Captain Pyo serves four times in a row.)

572
00:28:57,017 --> 00:28:58,585
(It's a targeted shot once again!)

573
00:28:59,353 --> 00:29:00,688
(Will it go outside again this time?)

574
00:29:00,998 --> 00:29:02,290
This is a chance!

575
00:29:07,494 --> 00:29:09,629
(Kokoro, stop!)

576
00:29:16,020 --> 00:29:18,004
- They score a point on the serve!
- They score a point on the serve!

577
00:29:21,742 --> 00:29:23,611
(The serve ace, Pyo Seung Ju)

578
00:29:24,645 --> 00:29:26,647
(Our captain is crazy!)

579
00:29:28,415 --> 00:29:31,318
(Beaming)

580
00:29:31,570 --> 00:29:34,632
They gave up 5 points,
but fought back with 5!

581
00:29:34,788 --> 00:29:37,724
(It's tied at 5 to 5.)

582
00:29:45,199 --> 00:29:47,701
(Admiring)

583
00:29:49,770 --> 00:29:52,539
Just as usual, we're playing too lightly.

584
00:29:53,340 --> 00:29:55,342
(The atmosphere at the bench
of Shujitsu High School is serious.)

585
00:29:55,375 --> 00:29:57,745
Why do they keep going like this?

586
00:29:59,980 --> 00:30:02,316
Chase the ball more aggressively.

587
00:30:02,349 --> 00:30:04,885
- Yes, ma'am!
- Yes, ma'am!

588
00:30:05,285 --> 00:30:09,022
(Fully tenacious)

589
00:30:09,990 --> 00:30:12,893
(The air feels somewhat different.)

590
00:30:14,561 --> 00:30:16,430
(Firstly, she delivers a targeted serve.)

591
00:30:17,831 --> 00:30:20,867
Legs! From your legs!

592
00:30:21,068 --> 00:30:22,670
(Everyone quickly moves in perfect order.)

593
00:30:22,870 --> 00:30:24,705
(When one is tossing)

594
00:30:24,972 --> 00:30:27,935
(A questionable formation)

595
00:30:28,876 --> 00:30:31,078
Forward!

596
00:30:31,445 --> 00:30:32,313
(Storming forward)

597
00:30:32,646 --> 00:30:34,948
(What's going on?)

598
00:30:34,949 --> 00:30:36,613
It's coming. It'll land at the front!

599
00:30:36,614 --> 00:30:38,619
(Will they spike down the middle again?)

600
00:30:39,453 --> 00:30:42,523
(Left)

601
00:30:43,365 --> 00:30:45,598
They jump. It's a block out.

602
00:30:45,685 --> 00:30:47,678
It's coming. It'll land at the front!
It's the front C.

603
00:30:48,798 --> 00:30:49,798
My goodness.

604
00:30:50,798 --> 00:30:54,335
(What just flew past us?)

605
00:30:55,944 --> 00:30:59,239
All the Shujitsu High School players were
ready to attack right now.

606
00:31:00,174 --> 00:31:01,842
(When she tossed,)

607
00:31:02,042 --> 00:31:05,345
(They stormed in from all directions,
from the left, middle, right, and back.)

608
00:31:06,046 --> 00:31:09,283
(Four-player attack formation)

609
00:31:09,717 --> 00:31:12,186
(This strategy hides
their real attacking direction.)

610
00:31:12,953 --> 00:31:14,721
(First set, Shujitsu High School 8
: Wonder Dogs 6)

611
00:31:15,055 --> 00:31:16,790
(It's Myoung Hwa's turn,
Wonder Dog's serving king)

612
00:31:20,094 --> 00:31:21,996
(Did she manage to score?)

613
00:31:22,396 --> 00:31:23,597
Let's go!

614
00:31:24,131 --> 00:31:25,699
(The moment she tossed,)

615
00:31:25,992 --> 00:31:28,235
(they immediately formed
an attacking formation once again.)

616
00:31:28,736 --> 00:31:29,876
(Will it come to the left side this time?)

617
00:31:29,877 --> 00:31:31,582
Stay on the right side!

618
00:31:35,444 --> 00:31:37,812
A spike down the middle!
She scores a point.

619
00:31:40,943 --> 00:31:43,384
- I'm really sorry.
- No, it's okay.

620
00:31:43,409 --> 00:31:46,235
Seung Ju, there was a slight gap.
You should cover that up first.

621
00:31:51,254 --> 00:31:52,359
Nice!

622
00:31:54,087 --> 00:31:57,430
Now, Hiruma Miharu, back number one,
joins the court.

623
00:31:57,431 --> 00:32:00,133
(Number one, Hiruma Miharu, joins.)

624
00:32:00,706 --> 00:32:04,652
In their past three games, Hiruma,
their number one, has made...

625
00:32:05,179 --> 00:32:06,179
more than 100 attacks.

626
00:32:08,418 --> 00:32:10,577
She has the most possession of the ball.

627
00:32:11,245 --> 00:32:15,983
(She was the one who mentioned
the 3-0 win against Wonder Dogs.)

628
00:32:16,694 --> 00:32:19,252
Look at the net! Watch out!

629
00:32:22,523 --> 00:32:23,523
(First set, Shujitsu High School 9
: Wonder Dogs 7)

630
00:32:23,524 --> 00:32:24,738
Young In will serve.

631
00:32:25,659 --> 00:32:27,995
(Young In's serve)

632
00:32:30,526 --> 00:32:32,526
A back toss.
It's a strong spike from the right.

633
00:32:33,159 --> 00:32:34,325
(Hye In defends.)

634
00:32:34,326 --> 00:32:35,709
- She defended it.
- It was a nice defense.

635
00:32:36,625 --> 00:32:38,438
They get ready for an attack right away.
She pushed it.

636
00:32:39,524 --> 00:32:40,944
From the right side. They blocked!

637
00:32:44,011 --> 00:32:45,045
(Swift)

638
00:32:45,354 --> 00:32:46,064
(Back to the position)

639
00:32:46,065 --> 00:32:47,297
Shujitsu High School throws it high.

640
00:32:47,381 --> 00:32:50,150
(Which side will it be this time?)

641
00:32:50,593 --> 00:32:52,593
- It's an attack down the middle.
- Nice!

642
00:32:57,457 --> 00:33:00,961
(Number one, Hiruma Miharu)

643
00:33:02,558 --> 00:33:05,265
I'm impressed by what this high school
player has showcased in such a short time.

644
00:33:06,430 --> 00:33:08,823
- She actually saw them trying to block.
- Yes, that's right.

645
00:33:08,863 --> 00:33:10,518
It was very clever
how she cleared that shot.

646
00:33:11,551 --> 00:33:13,923
Why did you guys jump over there
when the ball was here?

647
00:33:13,924 --> 00:33:15,490
You should have moved further forward.

648
00:33:17,623 --> 00:33:19,022
You can't be locating yourselves
like that.

649
00:33:19,515 --> 00:33:21,515
All players from Shujitsu High School are
engaging in the offensive.

650
00:33:21,915 --> 00:33:23,553
It's forcing the Wonder Dogs players...

651
00:33:23,554 --> 00:33:25,785
to struggle
with their defensive positioning.

652
00:33:31,293 --> 00:33:32,626
I was a little bit baffled.

653
00:33:33,260 --> 00:33:36,563
But we also had strategies prepared
to handle this situation.

654
00:33:37,392 --> 00:33:38,419
We're going all out on offense.

655
00:33:39,252 --> 00:33:41,971
Blocking will be the key to victory.

656
00:33:43,171 --> 00:33:45,538
You guys on the sides will both start
further inside today.

657
00:33:46,137 --> 00:33:47,357
Let me tell you why.

658
00:33:47,884 --> 00:33:49,910
When the toss from this side is too short,
you need to come and help them.

659
00:33:51,797 --> 00:33:53,814
And it's easier to come over to this side
when the shot is too long.

660
00:33:56,336 --> 00:33:57,590
For this Korea-Japan match,

661
00:33:58,162 --> 00:34:01,354
I've got some plans ready.

662
00:34:03,226 --> 00:34:05,319
Hey, we need someone right over here.

663
00:34:05,320 --> 00:34:07,260
(He'll be acting
as Shujitsu High School's number three.)

664
00:34:07,294 --> 00:34:10,364
(He'll be acting
as Shujitsu High School's number one.)

665
00:34:11,103 --> 00:34:12,397
(Customized training
regarding each attacker)

666
00:34:12,423 --> 00:34:13,917
Nice. Myoung Hwa, good job.

667
00:34:14,524 --> 00:34:16,971
Inside. That's right.

668
00:34:17,053 --> 00:34:19,304
Myoung Hwa, don't jump
too much. Try to stay straigh.

669
00:34:19,305 --> 00:34:21,024
(Will her carefully-planned strategies
pay off?)

670
00:34:21,942 --> 00:34:24,111
(First set, Shujitsu High School 11
: Wonder Dogs 9)

671
00:34:26,613 --> 00:34:29,049
(Who will get the toss this time?)

672
00:34:29,449 --> 00:34:30,617
To the left!

673
00:34:31,023 --> 00:34:32,023
To the left!

674
00:34:32,343 --> 00:34:33,843
Number six is there.

675
00:34:34,003 --> 00:34:36,003
Number six is there.

676
00:34:38,058 --> 00:34:40,594
(Peekaboo!)

677
00:34:44,058 --> 00:34:45,892
(Attacking to avoid the blockers)

678
00:34:45,893 --> 00:34:46,960
It's out!

679
00:34:48,629 --> 00:34:49,762
It's out!

680
00:34:49,897 --> 00:34:51,798
Nice!

681
00:34:52,666 --> 00:34:54,100
Let's go! Nice work!

682
00:34:54,168 --> 00:34:55,268
Nice, it's out!

683
00:34:55,536 --> 00:34:58,004
(Satisfied)

684
00:34:58,706 --> 00:35:00,073
Coach Yeon Koung told the players...

685
00:35:00,074 --> 00:35:02,876
to check the opponent's offense
beforehand,

686
00:35:02,877 --> 00:35:04,244
and it's paying off!

687
00:35:06,229 --> 00:35:09,048
(Something feels wrong)

688
00:35:12,519 --> 00:35:14,620
(First set, Shujitsu High School 12
: Wonder Dogs 11)

689
00:35:16,357 --> 00:35:17,991
Zone three!

690
00:35:17,992 --> 00:35:20,260
Zone three. Focus more on zone three.

691
00:35:21,328 --> 00:35:23,829
(Adjusting her position)

692
00:35:31,238 --> 00:35:32,238
Left!

693
00:35:32,540 --> 00:35:33,974
Zone three!

694
00:35:34,508 --> 00:35:35,508
- My ball.
- Go!

695
00:35:36,177 --> 00:35:37,110
Go!

696
00:35:37,111 --> 00:35:39,412
(Tossed to zone three as expected)

697
00:35:41,882 --> 00:35:44,087
(Hello again!)

698
00:35:46,005 --> 00:35:47,605
(Spiking to the side of the block)

699
00:35:48,607 --> 00:35:50,074
(Nice defense)

700
00:35:50,075 --> 00:35:52,710
Spike, and they made the pass.
It's a chance to score!

701
00:35:52,711 --> 00:35:53,544
It's up!
(An attacking opportunity)

702
00:35:56,482 --> 00:35:57,615
(But the blockers are already there!)

703
00:35:58,350 --> 00:36:01,152
(Will the one-blocking tactic fail?)

704
00:36:02,087 --> 00:36:03,254
(Spike down the line)

705
00:36:03,255 --> 00:36:04,322
Spike!

706
00:36:04,556 --> 00:36:06,724
The ball lands inside the line!

707
00:36:09,795 --> 00:36:10,628
Nice!

708
00:36:11,530 --> 00:36:13,297
Young In! Young In!

709
00:36:13,499 --> 00:36:14,833
(Nice block)

710
00:36:14,967 --> 00:36:17,402
Seung Ju, you did great.

711
00:36:21,774 --> 00:36:25,310
Zone three. Focus more on zone three.

712
00:36:29,281 --> 00:36:31,549
(A shaky pass)

713
00:36:31,817 --> 00:36:32,550
Nice serve.

714
00:36:33,652 --> 00:36:34,685
(Shujitsu aiming to strike back)

715
00:36:34,686 --> 00:36:35,719
Zone three.

716
00:36:35,721 --> 00:36:36,554
(Moving to zone three)

717
00:36:38,390 --> 00:36:39,390
(Nice block!)

718
00:36:39,391 --> 00:36:41,158
- Nice!
- That's it!

719
00:36:42,528 --> 00:36:43,995
(Pushed the ball over in a hurry)

720
00:36:44,196 --> 00:36:45,963
- A free ball.
- It's a free ball for Wonder Dogs.

721
00:36:45,964 --> 00:36:48,332
Na Yeon sets it up,
and a spike from the right!

722
00:36:49,168 --> 00:36:50,802
(They made the pass!)

723
00:36:52,638 --> 00:36:55,106
(Ready to go)

724
00:36:55,574 --> 00:36:58,876
(Who will they aim for this time?)

725
00:37:01,580 --> 00:37:03,314
Zone 3. Go to zone 3!

726
00:37:09,087 --> 00:37:10,054
(Perfect block)

727
00:37:10,055 --> 00:37:11,389
They blocked in the middle!

728
00:37:12,825 --> 00:37:16,494
They blocked it! A comeback block!

729
00:37:19,865 --> 00:37:20,898
I'll join the block.

730
00:37:21,366 --> 00:37:22,132
Me too.

731
00:37:22,501 --> 00:37:24,802
(I told you.)

732
00:37:25,404 --> 00:37:28,673
(They made it to take the lead back
with a perfect strategy.)

733
00:37:28,674 --> 00:37:30,041
We're doing great!

734
00:37:30,509 --> 00:37:32,343
It's now 13 to 12.

735
00:37:32,611 --> 00:37:34,378
Wonder Dogs take the lead by one point.

736
00:37:35,781 --> 00:37:36,748
Myoung Hwa serves.

737
00:37:36,748 --> 00:37:37,982
(Serve queen on the momentum)

738
00:37:40,234 --> 00:37:41,058
(Her serve shakes them first,)

739
00:37:41,059 --> 00:37:42,519
That's hard to set, isn't it?

740
00:37:42,953 --> 00:37:44,013
Keep your eyes on player seven.

741
00:37:44,014 --> 00:37:45,025
(then Coach Kim is added,)

742
00:37:47,526 --> 00:37:49,360
- Block!
- They blocked it!

743
00:37:49,361 --> 00:37:51,462
Score! Another point for Wonder Dogs!

744
00:37:51,463 --> 00:37:53,764
(it becomes a point!)

745
00:37:56,397 --> 00:37:57,931
Myoung Hwa serves again.

746
00:37:59,940 --> 00:38:01,574
(Who will they aim for this time?)

747
00:38:01,702 --> 00:38:03,303
Watch the left!

748
00:38:05,606 --> 00:38:07,540
- That's right!
- Blocked it!

749
00:38:08,376 --> 00:38:11,511
(First set, Shujitsu High School 16
: Wonder Dogs 17)

750
00:38:11,512 --> 00:38:14,280
Young In! More to the center.

751
00:38:16,384 --> 00:38:18,885
Think before you move, girls!

752
00:38:20,027 --> 00:38:22,629
You could've dodged that block.

753
00:38:27,821 --> 00:38:29,321
Their libero is out.

754
00:38:29,830 --> 00:38:32,365
(The libero is out
according to the rotation rule.)

755
00:38:33,768 --> 00:38:34,501
My ball.
(Another chance to score?)

756
00:38:35,970 --> 00:38:37,704
- Toss it...
- And a quick attack in the middle.

757
00:38:40,108 --> 00:38:41,075
They made the pass.

758
00:38:45,513 --> 00:38:47,614
(Spike to Chae Rim
instead of tall Hyeon Jeong)

759
00:38:49,150 --> 00:38:51,419
(Well-earned point by Shujitsu)

760
00:38:51,420 --> 00:38:54,154
Shujitsu High takes the lead by one point.

761
00:38:55,089 --> 00:38:56,656
Kurakaki serves.

762
00:39:00,595 --> 00:39:02,529
It hits the net, but goes over.

763
00:39:04,232 --> 00:39:05,132
Spike!

764
00:39:06,501 --> 00:39:07,601
That was nice speed.

765
00:39:11,305 --> 00:39:12,672
(Back to formation)

766
00:39:17,045 --> 00:39:18,712
(Score!)

767
00:39:19,814 --> 00:39:22,249
(Aimed at Na Yeon,
where the block is lower)

768
00:39:22,984 --> 00:39:24,184
The block failed.

769
00:39:24,552 --> 00:39:27,621
The opponents are also attacking
the weaker block points.

770
00:39:29,390 --> 00:39:31,858
- We can't lose points in a row like this.
- Right.

771
00:39:32,627 --> 00:39:33,594
Move closer!

772
00:39:33,594 --> 00:39:35,462
Come this way. Closer.

773
00:39:35,463 --> 00:39:37,064
(Wonder Dogs lose momentum.)

774
00:39:37,398 --> 00:39:39,566
(Kurakaki Mao serving)

775
00:39:40,568 --> 00:39:42,102
- My!
- Na Yeon!

776
00:39:42,937 --> 00:39:43,870
They set it up.

777
00:39:45,339 --> 00:39:46,739
(Fast attack to the middle)

778
00:39:47,608 --> 00:39:48,841
(Iron wall defense)

779
00:39:50,444 --> 00:39:51,411
(Spike from the right)

780
00:39:51,412 --> 00:39:52,946
They set it up,

781
00:39:53,681 --> 00:39:55,849
and they push it over!

782
00:39:59,087 --> 00:40:00,654
(A whistle?)

783
00:40:02,323 --> 00:40:05,091
(Point to Shujitsu?)

784
00:40:05,092 --> 00:40:06,459
Why?

785
00:40:06,994 --> 00:40:09,362
(What just happened?)

786
00:40:12,066 --> 00:40:15,502
The referee calls
an over-the-net violation.

787
00:40:15,670 --> 00:40:17,237
I didn't go over the net! I didn't!

788
00:40:17,438 --> 00:40:18,938
What are you talking about? I didn't!

789
00:40:18,973 --> 00:40:21,374
- She didn't go over the net!
- She didn't!

790
00:40:23,044 --> 00:40:24,845
Shoot!

791
00:40:24,845 --> 00:40:26,345
- Sorry, but I saw it.
- The ball was pushed over!

792
00:40:26,481 --> 00:40:27,748
She didn't do it!

793
00:40:27,748 --> 00:40:31,351
It was on our side. It passed the net.

794
00:40:32,720 --> 00:40:34,788
- We don't have a video review today.
- No.

795
00:40:35,089 --> 00:40:36,489
No hit. No hit.

796
00:40:36,657 --> 00:40:38,858
I'm sorry. It's my call.

797
00:40:38,859 --> 00:40:40,727
(The call cannot be overturned.)

798
00:40:46,100 --> 00:40:49,369
(No touch)

799
00:40:49,737 --> 00:40:51,538
(Wonder Dogs look unsettled)

800
00:40:51,539 --> 00:40:52,672
This is ridiculous.

801
00:40:53,141 --> 00:40:55,476
It's okay, guys. Stay calm.

802
00:40:56,763 --> 00:40:59,598
Well, we should wrap up the situation...

803
00:40:59,599 --> 00:41:00,699
and move on.

804
00:41:01,616 --> 00:41:03,150
Hey, listen.

805
00:41:03,150 --> 00:41:05,885
We don't have video review today,
so we can't be sloppy.

806
00:41:05,886 --> 00:41:07,353
We have to be clear and precise.

807
00:41:07,755 --> 00:41:08,855
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

808
00:41:09,024 --> 00:41:10,990
Now is the moment to prioritize...

809
00:41:10,992 --> 00:41:13,927
accurate plays over flashy ones.

810
00:41:13,928 --> 00:41:16,029
(They need a decisive hit.)

811
00:41:16,030 --> 00:41:17,964
Zone one. Block it.

812
00:41:18,432 --> 00:41:21,534
(First set, Shujitsu High School 22
: Wonder Dogs 19)

813
00:41:23,204 --> 00:41:23,970
Watch out.

814
00:41:25,439 --> 00:41:27,941
(Set it to Seung Ju)

815
00:41:28,576 --> 00:41:29,776
(Powerful spike)

816
00:41:29,777 --> 00:41:30,744
Spike!

817
00:41:32,980 --> 00:41:35,982
(They saved it!)

818
00:41:36,050 --> 00:41:36,850
Nice pass.

819
00:41:37,185 --> 00:41:38,519
They save the ball.

820
00:41:39,420 --> 00:41:42,722
(A free ball for Wonder Dogs)

821
00:41:42,723 --> 00:41:43,756
Hey!

822
00:41:44,859 --> 00:41:45,826
(Rushing over)
Na Yeon.

823
00:41:46,761 --> 00:41:49,429
(The center is completely uncovered.)

824
00:41:49,964 --> 00:41:50,797
Jump!

825
00:41:51,599 --> 00:41:52,465
A soft touch.

826
00:41:52,700 --> 00:41:54,234
(A clever soft touch)

827
00:41:59,507 --> 00:42:00,073
(Whistle)

828
00:42:00,408 --> 00:42:01,241
Nice!

829
00:42:01,909 --> 00:42:02,976
(Point to Wonder Dogs)

830
00:42:03,277 --> 00:42:04,878
The referee calls a net violation.

831
00:42:06,447 --> 00:42:08,014
(Touched)

832
00:42:08,416 --> 00:42:10,884
(They touched the net while blocking.)

833
00:42:11,786 --> 00:42:13,086
Hey, guys.

834
00:42:13,087 --> 00:42:14,888
How are we going to play the free ball?

835
00:42:14,889 --> 00:42:15,857
We have to make this clear.

836
00:42:15,857 --> 00:42:18,291
If we keep doing this,
we'll make mistakes at a crucial time.

837
00:42:18,292 --> 00:42:19,626
- Yes.
- Stay focused.

838
00:42:20,494 --> 00:42:21,627
When you're on the court,

839
00:42:21,629 --> 00:42:24,464
you need an older player
or a leader who can...

840
00:42:24,532 --> 00:42:26,633
- be honest and criticize.
- Absolutely.

841
00:42:29,103 --> 00:42:31,404
- Zone one, then zone six.
- Song Hee serving.

842
00:42:31,405 --> 00:42:33,239
Zone one, then watch out for zone six.

843
00:42:36,377 --> 00:42:37,477
(Quick open attack from the start)

844
00:42:37,712 --> 00:42:38,512
Quick open.

845
00:42:39,046 --> 00:42:39,746
They block it.

846
00:42:41,249 --> 00:42:42,549
A spike from the right!

847
00:42:42,950 --> 00:42:44,284
They save the ball.

848
00:42:44,552 --> 00:42:45,452
Seung Ju!

849
00:42:46,320 --> 00:42:48,121
- Hit it!
- They toss it up!

850
00:42:48,689 --> 00:42:50,890
(Ball to Seung Ju again)

851
00:42:51,592 --> 00:42:54,260
(They need one big play.)

852
00:43:00,634 --> 00:43:02,335
Spike!

853
00:43:02,336 --> 00:43:04,037
Touch out point for Wonder Dogs!

854
00:43:11,045 --> 00:43:12,779
Let's go one more time.

855
00:43:13,981 --> 00:43:16,082
Come on. Let's do one more like that.

856
00:43:16,812 --> 00:43:19,247
They've created good flow and momentum.

857
00:43:19,262 --> 00:43:20,295
(Closing the gap fast)

858
00:43:23,233 --> 00:43:25,201
Go, Na Yeon! Go!

859
00:43:26,269 --> 00:43:27,836
Get the cover!

860
00:43:28,004 --> 00:43:29,538
Get the cover!

861
00:43:29,539 --> 00:43:30,439
An underhand set.

862
00:43:30,440 --> 00:43:31,473
(back to Seung Ju again)

863
00:43:33,376 --> 00:43:35,711
- Open spike!
- Nice!

864
00:43:36,512 --> 00:43:38,346
(Defense failed)

865
00:43:38,348 --> 00:43:39,848
We're catching up! Only one point apart!

866
00:43:48,258 --> 00:43:49,658
One more, guys. One more.

867
00:43:49,659 --> 00:43:51,827
This is our chance. We need one more.

868
00:43:53,730 --> 00:43:55,130
It's 22 to 23.

869
00:43:55,131 --> 00:43:57,633
- Now's the time to tie the score.
- It is.

870
00:44:00,303 --> 00:44:01,670
Na Yeon.

871
00:44:01,671 --> 00:44:03,338
(Signaling serve position)

872
00:44:03,339 --> 00:44:04,739
Hit it in between, okay?

873
00:44:04,741 --> 00:44:05,541
(Got it.)

874
00:44:08,277 --> 00:44:09,410
(Target zone)

875
00:44:11,914 --> 00:44:14,749
(The target serve worked,
and they're off to a shaky start.)

876
00:44:15,585 --> 00:44:17,653
(Barely managed pass)

877
00:44:18,154 --> 00:44:21,123
(but there's no one to take it!)

878
00:44:26,362 --> 00:44:28,930
Shujitsu made an error!

879
00:44:30,099 --> 00:44:33,201
(Finally, tied at 23 to 23.)

880
00:44:36,406 --> 00:44:38,006
It was a crucial moment,

881
00:44:38,075 --> 00:44:40,781
- and the opponents lost their focus too.
- Indeed.

882
00:44:41,157 --> 00:44:43,744
The score is 23 to 23, back to square one.

883
00:44:44,757 --> 00:44:45,997
The two points were crucial!

884
00:44:47,114 --> 00:44:48,897
(The server is Na Yeon.)

885
00:44:48,970 --> 00:44:50,886
Young In, make sure to position yourself
and hit the ball's center.

886
00:44:50,939 --> 00:44:52,399
(Reminding her of the blocking position)

887
00:44:52,700 --> 00:44:53,821
Hit the center of the ball.

888
00:44:59,725 --> 00:45:01,561
- That's it!
- Their reception is shaking.

889
00:45:01,562 --> 00:45:03,563
(Their reception is shaky from the start.)

890
00:45:05,711 --> 00:45:08,635
- They need to calm down.
- It's a good chance for the Wonder Dogs.

891
00:45:08,993 --> 00:45:09,993
They received it.

892
00:45:11,000 --> 00:45:12,000
And the ball is set!

893
00:45:14,675 --> 00:45:15,675
Hey!

894
00:45:16,683 --> 00:45:17,683
Hit it!

895
00:45:22,081 --> 00:45:23,550
(Shujitsu High starts
their counterattack.)

896
00:45:24,084 --> 00:45:26,286
(The overwhelming wall is jumping.)

897
00:45:35,295 --> 00:45:36,568
(Block successful)

898
00:45:36,569 --> 00:45:39,132
Block successful on the right-side spike.

899
00:45:39,205 --> 00:45:42,135
- The play of the day by Myoung Hwa!
- The play of the day by Myoung Hwa!

900
00:45:43,337 --> 00:45:47,675
(They finally turned the game around.)

901
00:45:56,309 --> 00:46:00,587
The miscommunication
on the signs earlier...

902
00:46:01,161 --> 00:46:03,940
made me flinch for a moment.

903
00:46:04,180 --> 00:46:05,983
"The play of the day
by Myoung Hwa" continues.

904
00:46:05,984 --> 00:46:07,620
Right.
Myoung Hwa should be at a crucial moment!

905
00:46:10,597 --> 00:46:14,267
(The Shujitsu supporters fell silent
after conceding consecutive points.)

906
00:46:14,972 --> 00:46:16,785
It is now the set point
for the Wonder Dogs.

907
00:46:16,786 --> 00:46:18,004
(First set, Shujitsu High 23
: Wonder Dogs 24)

908
00:46:18,802 --> 00:46:23,043
Check No.3, Young In,
and find the proper position.

909
00:46:23,110 --> 00:46:24,278
(Adjusting her position)

910
00:46:24,745 --> 00:46:26,814
(Na Yeon serves three times in a row.)

911
00:46:29,583 --> 00:46:33,353
(As expected, the ball is sent to No.3.)

912
00:46:33,516 --> 00:46:35,488
Check No.3, Young In,
and find the proper position.

913
00:46:42,322 --> 00:46:43,664
- Spike!
- Good!

914
00:46:48,502 --> 00:46:50,867
(Block successful)

915
00:46:50,900 --> 00:46:53,507
- Nice block!
- She did it!

916
00:46:53,566 --> 00:46:56,446
The Wonder Dogs takes the first set.

917
00:46:57,344 --> 00:47:00,280
(We won!)

918
00:47:01,214 --> 00:47:04,384
(Thrilling comeback victory)

919
00:47:04,517 --> 00:47:08,855
(Crushing defeat after losing the lead)

920
00:47:10,017 --> 00:47:12,525
It would be hard
to stage a story like this...

921
00:47:12,897 --> 00:47:14,809
even if you tried.

922
00:47:14,823 --> 00:47:20,367
Seung Ju scored a total of 8 points
with a 55 percent attack success rate,

923
00:47:20,555 --> 00:47:22,915
and with two crucial blocks by Myoung Hwa,

924
00:47:22,955 --> 00:47:27,307
the Wonder Dogs takes the first set
in a thrilling comeback victory!

925
00:47:27,308 --> 00:47:29,242
(First set, Shujitsu High 23
: Wonder Dogs 25)

926
00:47:29,609 --> 00:47:32,045
(Timeout for the second set)

927
00:47:33,908 --> 00:47:37,168
Our team is really targeting
their serves well right now,

928
00:47:37,169 --> 00:47:39,325
so keep it up, just like now.

929
00:47:40,089 --> 00:47:44,210
And keep hitting the ball sharply
between the opponents like you are doing.

930
00:47:46,239 --> 00:47:50,617
Keep pressuring them harder and stronger.

931
00:47:50,618 --> 00:47:53,948
And they can defend all of our light taps,

932
00:47:54,288 --> 00:47:55,494
- so we must hit it hard.
- Okay.

933
00:47:55,495 --> 00:47:56,687
- Young In, you too.
- I will.

934
00:47:57,637 --> 00:48:00,983
(Let's push them back
with our strong attacks.)

935
00:48:02,088 --> 00:48:05,425
(When the Wonder Dogs
finished their timeout,)

936
00:48:06,153 --> 00:48:09,490
(silence fell on the Shujitsu players.)

937
00:48:16,375 --> 00:48:20,079
(The silence continues.)

938
00:48:21,012 --> 00:48:23,114
(After losing the first set,)

939
00:48:23,597 --> 00:48:26,366
(their mood has noticeably cooled.)

940
00:48:27,834 --> 00:48:31,338
It's only natural for the opponents
to set the ball to their ace.

941
00:48:31,471 --> 00:48:32,906
No matter how many times they attack,

942
00:48:32,939 --> 00:48:36,410
keep covering and keep the ball alive.

943
00:48:37,044 --> 00:48:39,446
Play while anticipating their moves.

944
00:48:41,940 --> 00:48:45,877
- As I always say,
- Yes.

945
00:48:46,820 --> 00:48:50,057
just cover the ball properly.

946
00:48:51,925 --> 00:48:54,895
(Let's strengthen our defense.)

947
00:49:00,534 --> 00:49:03,036
(The court is filled with tension.)

948
00:49:03,662 --> 00:49:07,032
(The Wonder Dogs on the attack)

949
00:49:07,641 --> 00:49:10,244
(Shujitsu High on defense)

950
00:49:10,510 --> 00:49:12,665
(A battle of spear and shield)

951
00:49:12,691 --> 00:49:15,915
Now, the second set begins
with the Wonder Dogs' serve.

952
00:49:15,916 --> 00:49:18,518
(Second set, Shujitsu High 0
: Wonder Dogs 0)

953
00:49:22,248 --> 00:49:23,530
The reception is shaky.

954
00:49:24,691 --> 00:49:26,126
(But the underhand set is steady.)

955
00:49:29,309 --> 00:49:30,363
They saved the ball.

956
00:49:34,634 --> 00:49:36,870
(This is a chance!)

957
00:49:38,839 --> 00:49:42,343
(Chae Rim's powerful spike)

958
00:49:42,709 --> 00:49:44,744
(But Senba Kokoro blocks it right away.)

959
00:49:47,114 --> 00:49:49,883
(Neck-and-neck)

960
00:49:50,276 --> 00:49:51,818
Again, it's a high ball.

961
00:49:51,852 --> 00:49:53,654
(It's a hard-won chance again.)

962
00:49:54,554 --> 00:49:56,022
Get ready and watch.

963
00:49:56,723 --> 00:49:59,693
(They're jumping at the same time!)

964
00:50:02,964 --> 00:50:04,744
It's blocked!

965
00:50:07,110 --> 00:50:09,803
Shujitsu High's perfect defense
leads to a point.

966
00:50:10,770 --> 00:50:13,506
(Smiling)

967
00:50:13,907 --> 00:50:16,510
(Second set, Shujitsu High 1
: Wonder Dogs 1)

968
00:50:17,144 --> 00:50:19,980
(The game continues.)

969
00:50:23,116 --> 00:50:25,385
(Stable reception)

970
00:50:25,919 --> 00:50:27,721
Back toss.

971
00:50:28,527 --> 00:50:31,295
- Spike.
- That was a clean hit.

972
00:50:32,094 --> 00:50:34,544
Their precise reception
resulted in a score.

973
00:50:37,105 --> 00:50:38,840
(The ball was directed
accurately to the setter.)

974
00:50:39,699 --> 00:50:43,495
(A clean toss set up a successful attack.)

975
00:50:44,337 --> 00:50:46,206
(With Shujitsu High's point,)

976
00:50:46,673 --> 00:50:49,509
(the momentum of the supporters rose.)

977
00:50:50,177 --> 00:50:53,080
(Shujitsu High's defense has changed.)

978
00:50:53,713 --> 00:50:55,415
(The game continues.)

979
00:50:56,712 --> 00:50:57,885
Nice.

980
00:50:58,318 --> 00:50:59,686
(Neat defense)

981
00:51:01,188 --> 00:51:03,323
(Perfect two-step connection)

982
00:51:09,596 --> 00:51:12,599
(Their defense
continuously leads to points.)

983
00:51:12,797 --> 00:51:16,102
(Second set, Shujitsu High 3
: Wonder Dogs 2)

984
00:51:17,637 --> 00:51:21,608
(Shujitsu High's defense is more solid
than I thought.)

985
00:51:22,709 --> 00:51:26,846
(If they come out with a strong defense,)

986
00:51:27,308 --> 00:51:29,688
We must focus on attacking even more now.

987
00:51:30,317 --> 00:51:33,587
(we break through
with even stronger attacks.)

988
00:51:38,423 --> 00:51:39,423
Seung Ju.

989
00:51:42,406 --> 00:51:43,663
She's targeting the center!

990
00:51:44,464 --> 00:51:46,466
(Their defense finally started shaking.)

991
00:51:49,069 --> 00:51:50,570
She threw herself to save the ball!

992
00:51:51,549 --> 00:51:53,974
Get ready. It's a chance.

993
00:51:55,065 --> 00:51:56,643
They sent the ball over.

994
00:52:01,075 --> 00:52:02,149
Hit it!

995
00:52:05,919 --> 00:52:08,088
(But is the ball flying over Hyeon Jeong?)

996
00:52:08,121 --> 00:52:12,192
(The real hit goes...)

997
00:52:13,860 --> 00:52:17,363
(from here!)

998
00:52:19,092 --> 00:52:22,324
- That's it. Nice play.
- She hit it hard!

999
00:52:22,902 --> 00:52:25,271
(Second set, Shujitsu High 3
: Wonder Dogs 3)

1000
00:52:27,648 --> 00:52:30,050
(After Hyeon Jeong faked
out the opponent,)

1001
00:52:30,236 --> 00:52:32,312
(Chae Rim's powerful hit
followed immediately.)

1002
00:52:32,912 --> 00:52:35,581
(The middle blocker, deceived
by Hyeon Jeong, couldn't keep up.)

1003
00:52:36,316 --> 00:52:39,319
(Shujitsu High's defense is pierced...)

1004
00:52:40,060 --> 00:52:43,230
(by the fast, penetrating attack.)

1005
00:52:43,690 --> 00:52:46,860
(Eventually, the Wonder Dogs equalizes.)

1006
00:52:47,694 --> 00:52:51,331
(The game is tied.)

1007
00:52:53,833 --> 00:52:55,234
Do not wander around on the court.

1008
00:52:55,260 --> 00:52:58,563
Stand in your position!

1009
00:52:59,239 --> 00:53:02,642
(Strengthening the defense again)

1010
00:53:06,780 --> 00:53:08,582
(The blockers are right
in front of the net...)

1011
00:53:08,915 --> 00:53:10,950
(while the defenders are
positioned in the back.)

1012
00:53:11,284 --> 00:53:13,253
(Shujitsu High reorganized
their defensive formation.)

1013
00:53:16,056 --> 00:53:18,592
(The game continues.)

1014
00:53:24,837 --> 00:53:26,909
She tried to poke the ball through,
but the center was blocked.

1015
00:53:27,503 --> 00:53:28,802
Shoot.

1016
00:53:29,703 --> 00:53:32,309
We can do nothing about what they do well.

1017
00:53:32,310 --> 00:53:33,607
(Point from the block)

1018
00:53:39,586 --> 00:53:40,652
(Their strong defense continues.)

1019
00:53:40,652 --> 00:53:41,935
They kept the ball alive.

1020
00:53:46,754 --> 00:53:48,674
Back attack through the center.

1021
00:53:50,015 --> 00:53:52,291
Shujitsu High's defense is
getting tighter and tighter.

1022
00:53:52,818 --> 00:53:53,964
(Their defense is way too strong.)

1023
00:53:53,983 --> 00:53:55,495
We can't let them take control like this.

1024
00:53:57,630 --> 00:53:59,665
She saved the ball.

1025
00:53:59,794 --> 00:54:01,534
And it's set right away. Spike!

1026
00:54:01,535 --> 00:54:03,737
(Shujitsu High's offense is
firing on all cylinders now.)

1027
00:54:05,138 --> 00:54:08,041
(In no time, it's a four-point gap.)

1028
00:54:08,643 --> 00:54:11,778
The Wonder Dogs can't break
through Shujitsu High's defense at all.

1029
00:54:12,912 --> 00:54:15,782
(Technical timeout)

1030
00:54:17,282 --> 00:54:18,318
Hey.

1031
00:54:19,286 --> 00:54:20,814
(She takes a quick look at Shujitsu.)

1032
00:54:21,369 --> 00:54:25,206
Their defensive line keeps staying deep.

1033
00:54:25,786 --> 00:54:28,899
Try a soft tip each time.

1034
00:54:29,086 --> 00:54:30,657
And use your specialty, the middle push.

1035
00:54:30,831 --> 00:54:31,925
- Okay.
- Try it.

1036
00:54:33,226 --> 00:54:36,329
(The rookie coach was watching
Shujitsu's court carefully.)

1037
00:54:38,117 --> 00:54:41,013
(She noticed that the defenders were
positioned deep in the back.)

1038
00:54:42,024 --> 00:54:44,424
(Their center defense is relatively weak.)

1039
00:54:44,790 --> 00:54:46,257
You can push or tip to zone three.

1040
00:54:46,524 --> 00:54:48,024
- Hit it softly.
- Yes, Coach.

1041
00:54:48,190 --> 00:54:49,190
Let's go.

1042
00:54:53,290 --> 00:54:55,424
(They become determined
as they go back to the court.)

1043
00:54:55,424 --> 00:54:57,157
Get the ball first!

1044
00:55:00,959 --> 00:55:02,959
Losing the game is my worst fear.

1045
00:55:03,393 --> 00:55:05,493
And the same goes for our team.

1046
00:55:06,293 --> 00:55:09,726
I believe we absolutely can't lose.

1047
00:55:10,193 --> 00:55:11,693
When it comes to a Korea-Japan match,

1048
00:55:11,826 --> 00:55:14,493
we must win at all costs.

1049
00:55:16,193 --> 00:55:19,459
Wonder Dogs need to stop
their opponents' flow now.

1050
00:55:19,459 --> 00:55:21,459
(Can this strategy be
their turning point?)

1051
00:55:21,459 --> 00:55:23,959
(The game restarts.)

1052
00:55:26,893 --> 00:55:28,326
(Good reception)

1053
00:55:29,726 --> 00:55:30,893
(Trying a push shot right away)

1054
00:55:30,893 --> 00:55:31,993
She pushed the ball.

1055
00:55:33,393 --> 00:55:34,559
They defended well.

1056
00:55:40,059 --> 00:55:42,193
(The ball is on their side again.)

1057
00:55:42,193 --> 00:55:43,526
Koo Hye In's second contact.

1058
00:55:43,526 --> 00:55:45,393
(Their middle zone is empty now?)

1059
00:55:45,526 --> 00:55:47,159
(It follows Coach Kim's strategy.)

1060
00:55:48,993 --> 00:55:50,759
Pyo Seung Ju pushes the ball
to zone three!

1061
00:55:50,759 --> 00:55:52,993
(Realizing late)

1062
00:55:54,626 --> 00:55:56,259
(Breaks through their defense)

1063
00:55:56,259 --> 00:55:57,926
The ball landed on the ground.

1064
00:55:58,659 --> 00:56:01,693
(Second set, Shujitsu High School 8 :
Wonder Dogs 5)

1065
00:56:01,693 --> 00:56:03,659
For Pyo Seung Ju,

1066
00:56:04,126 --> 00:56:06,726
- her playing style was totally strategic.
- That's right.

1067
00:56:08,826 --> 00:56:12,826
She tipped the ball to an empty spot
after examining their defense line.

1068
00:56:12,893 --> 00:56:15,326
She aimed flawlessly
at the undefended middle zone.

1069
00:56:15,693 --> 00:56:19,126
Seung Ju played
according to Coach Kim's strategy.

1070
00:56:19,393 --> 00:56:20,426
That's it, Seung Ju!

1071
00:56:20,426 --> 00:56:21,459
(Satisfied)

1072
00:56:21,459 --> 00:56:22,459
Way to go!

1073
00:56:24,859 --> 00:56:28,526
(The game continues.)

1074
00:56:30,093 --> 00:56:31,093
Seung Ju tips it.

1075
00:56:31,859 --> 00:56:34,026
- A direct spike!
- Nice play!

1076
00:56:34,626 --> 00:56:37,026
(Pyo Seung Ju scores again.)

1077
00:56:37,326 --> 00:56:39,226
(Even for a quick attack,)

1078
00:56:39,226 --> 00:56:40,926
- She saved it.
- It's a nice toss.

1079
00:56:40,926 --> 00:56:42,059
Nice play!

1080
00:56:42,059 --> 00:56:43,593
(Perfect execution)

1081
00:56:44,059 --> 00:56:46,759
(Seung Ju continues to rise.)

1082
00:56:49,259 --> 00:56:52,159
Keep following the ball!

1083
00:56:52,459 --> 00:56:55,159
We can really see
that she's experienced...

1084
00:56:55,493 --> 00:56:57,959
- in the match today.
- Exactly.

1085
00:56:57,959 --> 00:56:59,626
The more it falls,
the more you hit it inside.

1086
00:56:59,626 --> 00:57:00,659
Great job.

1087
00:57:03,226 --> 00:57:06,359
(The Wonder Dogs are catching up.)

1088
00:57:11,026 --> 00:57:16,459
(We must break through.)

1089
00:57:17,026 --> 00:57:21,859
(We must block them.)

1090
00:57:22,093 --> 00:57:24,526
(The battle of attack and defense is
getting fiercer.)

1091
00:57:30,359 --> 00:57:31,626
The reception is shaky.

1092
00:57:31,626 --> 00:57:32,893
(An unstable reception from the start)

1093
00:57:32,893 --> 00:57:34,093
Move in!

1094
00:57:34,626 --> 00:57:36,493
(Barely attempting an attack
in the middle)

1095
00:57:37,093 --> 00:57:38,893
(Senba immediately blocks it.)

1096
00:57:39,359 --> 00:57:41,026
(The ball is tossed right to the setter.)

1097
00:57:42,426 --> 00:57:43,426
She saved it!

1098
00:57:45,859 --> 00:57:48,059
(Baek Chae Rim tries to spike.)

1099
00:57:48,959 --> 00:57:50,793
Quick. Get ready to defend!

1100
00:57:53,659 --> 00:57:55,326
(The middle blocker catches up quickly.)

1101
00:57:55,893 --> 00:57:57,659
(Defenders are at the front.)

1102
00:57:58,093 --> 00:57:59,526
(The libero is on the cross-court.)

1103
00:57:59,893 --> 00:58:02,559
(Their defense formation is stronger.)

1104
00:58:07,293 --> 00:58:08,559
(Senba blocks it again.)

1105
00:58:08,559 --> 00:58:10,093
She saves the ball again!

1106
00:58:14,893 --> 00:58:16,759
It's blocked at the right.

1107
00:58:16,759 --> 00:58:18,426
(That's it!)

1108
00:58:18,426 --> 00:58:20,559
(The fierce battle goes on.)

1109
00:58:21,926 --> 00:58:22,959
Attacking on the right again.

1110
00:58:27,259 --> 00:58:28,726
She dives to save the ball!

1111
00:58:30,926 --> 00:58:32,993
(Baek Chae Rim's another push shot)

1112
00:58:33,293 --> 00:58:34,293
It's pushed far.

1113
00:58:34,293 --> 00:58:36,193
(The middle zone is empty.)

1114
00:58:36,759 --> 00:58:38,459
(Shujitsu High School's solid defense)

1115
00:58:40,793 --> 00:58:41,793
She runs!

1116
00:58:46,626 --> 00:58:47,893
(Out)

1117
00:58:47,893 --> 00:58:49,659
It's out.

1118
00:58:51,226 --> 00:58:54,359
(After a long battle,)

1119
00:58:55,893 --> 00:58:57,759
(the Wonder Dogs score.)

1120
00:58:57,759 --> 00:58:59,626
The players are doing great...

1121
00:58:59,626 --> 00:59:02,093
at calmly breaking
through the defensive line.

1122
00:59:02,093 --> 00:59:03,326
(A strategic play...)

1123
00:59:03,759 --> 00:59:06,726
(that found the weak spot
in their defense.)

1124
00:59:07,072 --> 00:59:08,072
Nice one!

1125
00:59:09,946 --> 00:59:11,041
It's 10 to 12.

1126
00:59:11,042 --> 00:59:12,479
(Shujitsu High School 12 : Wonder Dogs 10)

1127
00:59:13,459 --> 00:59:15,793
(The game continues.)

1128
00:59:16,759 --> 00:59:18,093
Baek Chae Rim receives it.

1129
00:59:19,793 --> 00:59:21,793
(A push shot to the middle again)

1130
00:59:24,893 --> 00:59:26,359
(She fails to defend.)

1131
00:59:26,513 --> 00:59:30,113
The Wonder Dogs score by aiming
at their opponents' weakness in defense.

1132
00:59:30,659 --> 00:59:32,926
Pyo Seung Ju uses
as little strength as possible...

1133
00:59:33,093 --> 00:59:37,059
and targets their weak spot perfectly.

1134
00:59:37,059 --> 00:59:38,893
(Shujitsu High School 14 : Wonder Dogs 13)

1135
00:59:38,926 --> 00:59:41,293
(The Wonder Dogs close the gap
to one point.)

1136
00:59:41,793 --> 00:59:44,793
(Kim Hyeon Jeong serves,
following the momentum.)

1137
00:59:48,426 --> 00:59:50,259
(An unstable reception)

1138
00:59:53,326 --> 00:59:54,326
Spike!

1139
00:59:54,593 --> 00:59:56,693
- She blocked it. Na Yeon sets!
- The ball is saved.

1140
00:59:56,693 --> 00:59:58,093
(Tossing far to Seung Ju)

1141
00:59:58,093 --> 00:59:59,093
Hit it!

1142
01:00:02,226 --> 01:00:04,093
(A perfect setup to spike)

1143
01:00:09,493 --> 01:00:11,759
(She succeeds to attack
with a sudden tip.)

1144
01:00:12,126 --> 01:00:13,793
(Shujitsu High School 14 : Wonder Dogs 14)

1145
01:00:13,793 --> 01:00:15,693
We should give a hand for this.

1146
01:00:15,859 --> 01:00:19,493
(You're the best, Seung Ju!)

1147
01:00:20,493 --> 01:00:21,926
(Coach Kim applauds too.)

1148
01:00:22,459 --> 01:00:25,193
(It's now a tie, thanks to Seung Ju.)

1149
01:00:25,693 --> 01:00:29,693
Pyo Seung Ju is leading the team,
whether she plays strongly or softly.

1150
01:00:29,978 --> 01:00:31,144
She's like a maestro.

1151
01:00:31,226 --> 01:00:34,959
She knows all the defense patterns
of the opposing team.

1152
01:00:34,959 --> 01:00:36,095
(Maestro Pyo leads in the front.)

1153
01:00:36,222 --> 01:00:37,222
It's a tie.

1154
01:00:37,226 --> 01:00:38,326
(Kim Hyeon Jeong serves again.)

1155
01:00:40,293 --> 01:00:41,326
(The setter tries to counterattack.)

1156
01:00:41,326 --> 01:00:42,426
(Where will she toss it?)

1157
01:00:42,693 --> 01:00:43,893
Number two!

1158
01:00:43,893 --> 01:00:44,893
Inside!

1159
01:00:46,826 --> 01:00:48,693
(She chooses a back C to number one.)

1160
01:00:49,659 --> 01:00:50,659
A back C!

1161
01:00:52,426 --> 01:00:53,459
Will they block?

1162
01:00:53,459 --> 01:00:54,926
(They blocked it!)

1163
01:00:55,159 --> 01:00:58,993
(She reads their attacks
like sheet music.)

1164
01:00:59,393 --> 01:01:01,259
(Under Maestro Pyo's lead)

1165
01:01:01,593 --> 01:01:03,759
(Shujitsu High School 14 : Wonder Dogs 15)

1166
01:01:03,759 --> 01:01:05,359
That is Pyo Seung Ju!

1167
01:01:05,726 --> 01:01:08,659
It's like we're watching a match
at the Tokyo Olympics!

1168
01:01:09,800 --> 01:01:14,633
(From spikes to tips and blocking)

1169
01:01:14,633 --> 01:01:18,367
Seung Ju was in the team
that reached the semifinals.

1170
01:01:18,400 --> 01:01:21,567
She was one of the players
along with Coach Kim.

1171
01:01:23,800 --> 01:01:25,467
Koo Hye In receives the ball to save it.

1172
01:01:25,467 --> 01:01:27,533
(Go for it, Maestro Pyo!)

1173
01:01:28,233 --> 01:01:29,333
(A spike this time)

1174
01:01:30,067 --> 01:01:31,233
Spike!

1175
01:01:32,100 --> 01:01:34,233
(Let the music play!)

1176
01:01:34,607 --> 01:01:36,873
(The Wonder Dogs are on a roll.)

1177
01:01:37,500 --> 01:01:38,833
Yes!

1178
01:01:39,100 --> 01:01:41,833
Seung Ju! Pyo Seung Ju!

1179
01:01:41,833 --> 01:01:43,136
(Chuckling)

1180
01:01:43,473 --> 01:01:45,518
(Thanks to Maestro Pyo's skillful play,)

1181
01:01:45,519 --> 01:01:48,819
(Shujitsu High School is
completely overwhelmed.)

1182
01:01:49,333 --> 01:01:50,867
Nice toss, Na Yeon.

1183
01:01:52,747 --> 01:01:55,347
(A technical timeout)

1184
01:01:56,626 --> 01:02:00,033
They're not doing anything different.
It's just the same.

1185
01:02:00,133 --> 01:02:02,933
You only need to prevent errors
from basic moves.

1186
01:02:03,167 --> 01:02:05,400
We have to get more points.

1187
01:02:05,433 --> 01:02:07,267
We should continue to score.

1188
01:02:07,300 --> 01:02:10,733
And you can't just stay still
when they receive the ball and hit back.

1189
01:02:10,767 --> 01:02:12,233
- Someone has to send it up.
- Understood.

1190
01:02:12,632 --> 01:02:14,999
(Let's secure this lead.)

1191
01:02:16,167 --> 01:02:18,874
Each of you has to do your job properly.

1192
01:02:18,875 --> 01:02:22,867
You struggle because you miss
the decisive point to score.

1193
01:02:22,867 --> 01:02:25,133
You're supposed to earn that point.

1194
01:02:25,133 --> 01:02:28,400
If each of you properly did your work,

1195
01:02:28,401 --> 01:02:30,367
this would have been a piece of cake.

1196
01:02:30,500 --> 01:02:33,200
Some of you are in trouble
because you didn't block properly.

1197
01:02:33,453 --> 01:02:36,287
Your teammates at the back struggle
due to poor receptions.

1198
01:02:36,288 --> 01:02:38,978
Those at the front struggle
because of poor serve and reception.

1199
01:02:38,979 --> 01:02:41,179
Serve and receive the ball properly,
starting with me.

1200
01:02:42,700 --> 01:02:46,767
You must score this time.

1201
01:02:48,873 --> 01:02:51,773
(Shujitsu High School must break
this momentum.)

1202
01:02:52,331 --> 01:02:54,133
Let's do our job and be strong!

1203
01:02:54,133 --> 01:02:56,400
(Let's do this!)

1204
01:02:57,333 --> 01:03:00,600
(We'll score, no matter what!)

1205
01:03:00,733 --> 01:03:03,733
In the second set,
the Wonder Dogs have managed...

1206
01:03:03,967 --> 01:03:06,500
to take the lead back
with the score of 16 to 15.

1207
01:03:06,500 --> 01:03:07,820
(A tight, single-point gap)

1208
01:03:07,821 --> 01:03:09,521
Get ready with your legs first!

1209
01:03:10,033 --> 01:03:11,233
Do it calmly.

1210
01:03:11,706 --> 01:03:13,839
(We must seize the flow for victory.)

1211
01:03:13,840 --> 01:03:15,107
Let's go!

1212
01:03:16,105 --> 01:03:18,468
(Lee Na Yeon serves.)

1213
01:03:19,329 --> 01:03:20,263
Gosh, please!

1214
01:03:22,029 --> 01:03:23,896
(Well received!)

1215
01:03:23,896 --> 01:03:25,763
It came to the right side.
She received it well.

1216
01:03:26,829 --> 01:03:29,329
(Will number three jump?)

1217
01:03:29,329 --> 01:03:30,229
It's number three.

1218
01:03:31,763 --> 01:03:32,729
Go to the back!

1219
01:03:34,163 --> 01:03:35,829
(Right at that moment, number one leaps!)

1220
01:03:35,829 --> 01:03:36,929
Let's go!

1221
01:03:38,596 --> 01:03:39,396
It's a pipe.

1222
01:03:42,996 --> 01:03:43,996
It's a back-row attack to the center.

1223
01:03:43,996 --> 01:03:45,329
(She missed it.)

1224
01:03:49,615 --> 01:03:53,452
(Hiruma scores from a back attack.)

1225
01:03:54,828 --> 01:03:56,028
(Koharu is Hiruma's nickname.)

1226
01:03:56,029 --> 01:03:57,896
(It's tied again!)

1227
01:03:58,222 --> 01:04:01,055
(Let's go, Shujitsu High School!)

1228
01:04:02,029 --> 01:04:04,396
Hey, Myoung Hwa!

1229
01:04:04,396 --> 01:04:05,496
Number six is low.

1230
01:04:08,281 --> 01:04:10,648
(Shujitsu High School's number six is
short.)

1231
01:04:11,214 --> 01:04:13,014
(Is the wonder coach targeting
a lower spot?)

1232
01:04:15,914 --> 01:04:17,747
(Smooth connection)

1233
01:04:18,214 --> 01:04:19,547
(Hit a quick one!)

1234
01:04:22,080 --> 01:04:22,914
Na Yeon.

1235
01:04:23,714 --> 01:04:25,314
A quick attack to the floor!

1236
01:04:27,447 --> 01:04:29,680
(Number six is bewildered.)

1237
01:04:30,147 --> 01:04:32,780
(The wonder coach's strategy hit
the bull's eye.)

1238
01:04:33,714 --> 01:04:35,714
(Second set, Shujitsu High School 16
: Wonder Dogs 17)

1239
01:04:35,714 --> 01:04:37,580
Do it right away!

1240
01:04:39,047 --> 01:04:40,347
(The game continues.)

1241
01:04:40,347 --> 01:04:41,380
It's mine!

1242
01:04:41,747 --> 01:04:42,714
Chae Rim!

1243
01:04:42,714 --> 01:04:44,047
Seung Ju connects it with a set.

1244
01:04:44,048 --> 01:04:45,213
(Soft tip)

1245
01:04:45,214 --> 01:04:47,380
Nice try, but they defended.

1246
01:04:47,380 --> 01:04:48,847
To the right!

1247
01:04:48,847 --> 01:04:49,780
It's on the right side.

1248
01:04:49,780 --> 01:04:50,914
Blocking.

1249
01:04:51,514 --> 01:04:53,480
- Hey!
- Young In received it.

1250
01:04:56,014 --> 01:04:57,414
She rushed forward and smashed it!

1251
01:04:57,414 --> 01:04:59,714
(Did she miss it?)

1252
01:04:59,714 --> 01:05:00,614
Take your time!

1253
01:05:05,314 --> 01:05:07,180
(I won't...)

1254
01:05:07,180 --> 01:05:08,580
(let it go!)

1255
01:05:17,047 --> 01:05:18,447
(Nice one!)

1256
01:05:19,180 --> 01:05:24,047
(Second set, Shujitsu High School 17
: Wonder Dogs 19)

1257
01:05:24,347 --> 01:05:25,914
Na Yeon, toss it to the right.

1258
01:05:32,414 --> 01:05:33,814
(She tossed it to the right!)

1259
01:05:35,580 --> 01:05:36,780
Cover it!

1260
01:05:40,914 --> 01:05:42,947
(It blankly fell to an empty spot.)

1261
01:05:43,180 --> 01:05:44,880
(Lamenting)

1262
01:05:45,780 --> 01:05:47,147
She did it.

1263
01:05:47,147 --> 01:05:48,606
- They tied it with a block.
- They should've covered it.

1264
01:05:48,607 --> 01:05:50,080
It's Shujitsu High School's point.

1265
01:05:50,547 --> 01:05:52,347
(Thanks to the ace's great performance,)

1266
01:05:52,547 --> 01:05:54,947
(Shujitsu High School is
tenaciously chasing the Wonder Dogs.)

1267
01:05:57,780 --> 01:06:00,280
(Second set, Shujitsu High School 19
: Wonder Dogs 20)

1268
01:06:01,080 --> 01:06:03,980
(It's time to make a decision.)

1269
01:06:04,347 --> 01:06:05,214
Coach!

1270
01:06:08,247 --> 01:06:09,247
You have to block it.

1271
01:06:10,447 --> 01:06:12,047
Hey, Sol!

1272
01:06:12,047 --> 01:06:13,414
Make sure you block well.

1273
01:06:13,414 --> 01:06:14,680
The ball will come to the center.

1274
01:06:14,680 --> 01:06:16,147
Number one and two!

1275
01:06:16,680 --> 01:06:17,680
Sol, you should mark number one!

1276
01:06:19,914 --> 01:06:22,547
(Is Shujitsu High School's number one
their target to block?)

1277
01:06:23,114 --> 01:06:25,880
(When Na Yeon, who's relatively shorter,
is at the front,)

1278
01:06:27,280 --> 01:06:30,280
(Shujitsu High School attacks
from the left.)

1279
01:06:31,747 --> 01:06:34,221
(For the Wonder Dogs,
whose defense keeps getting broken...)

1280
01:06:34,222 --> 01:06:38,114
(by canon-like attacks
from Shujitsu High School,)

1281
01:06:38,684 --> 01:06:41,782
Sol, make sure you block well.
The ball will come to the center.

1282
01:06:41,789 --> 01:06:43,546
(the Wonder Coach executes a bold move.)

1283
01:06:43,913 --> 01:06:45,410
(The tall setter, Sol, is substituted in.)

1284
01:06:45,411 --> 01:06:48,014
To be honest, I hope the opponents
would play in front of Sol...

1285
01:06:48,014 --> 01:06:50,214
- so she could score with a block.
- Tell me about it.

1286
01:06:50,814 --> 01:06:53,414
(Since the very first match,)

1287
01:06:54,114 --> 01:06:56,847
(Sol has either been cheering
from the warm-up zone...)

1288
01:06:56,847 --> 01:06:59,347
(or quietly warming up in the corner...)

1289
01:06:59,347 --> 01:07:01,980
(as a backup setter.)

1290
01:07:03,414 --> 01:07:08,580
(Will the Wonder Coach's strategy
of changing players pay off?)

1291
01:07:11,014 --> 01:07:11,747
(Shaky)

1292
01:07:12,347 --> 01:07:13,347
The receiver is shaken.

1293
01:07:13,347 --> 01:07:15,347
- Now, this is a chance.
- Number two sends it over.

1294
01:07:15,347 --> 01:07:16,647
Hit it!

1295
01:07:17,214 --> 01:07:18,247
You have to do it well!

1296
01:07:19,247 --> 01:07:21,847
(Will she get a chance to toss
before she even gets to block?)

1297
01:07:22,047 --> 01:07:23,280
Sol, nice toss!

1298
01:07:28,747 --> 01:07:30,447
- That's great.
- A spike!

1299
01:07:30,447 --> 01:07:32,447
She smashed that ball down!

1300
01:07:35,580 --> 01:07:38,114
(The point was from Sol's set.)

1301
01:07:38,380 --> 01:07:40,080
(What just happened?)

1302
01:07:40,314 --> 01:07:42,014
Nice toss!

1303
01:07:44,114 --> 01:07:45,714
(Feeling proud)

1304
01:07:46,680 --> 01:07:47,814
Sol, that's it.

1305
01:07:47,814 --> 01:07:48,847
(Good job, Sol.)

1306
01:07:49,847 --> 01:07:52,747
Coach Kim sent her out to block,

1307
01:07:52,747 --> 01:07:55,080
- and she showcased an excellent set.
- That's right.

1308
01:07:55,080 --> 01:07:58,947
It was a perfect quick set for a spike.

1309
01:07:58,947 --> 01:08:01,214
(Sol is a setter too.)

1310
01:08:01,580 --> 01:08:02,947
Now, the score is 21 to 19.

1311
01:08:02,947 --> 01:08:03,980
(Young In's serve)

1312
01:08:05,747 --> 01:08:06,647
They're jumping.

1313
01:08:07,480 --> 01:08:08,580
- A block!
- Blocking.

1314
01:08:09,414 --> 01:08:10,647
- That's right.
- The ball is rebounded.

1315
01:08:10,647 --> 01:08:11,514
Sol!

1316
01:08:12,347 --> 01:08:13,680
- Spike!
- Cover it!

1317
01:08:15,314 --> 01:08:16,514
They're tossing it.

1318
01:08:16,514 --> 01:08:18,647
It went over to the other court.
It's another free ball for Young In.

1319
01:08:18,647 --> 01:08:20,214
Go!

1320
01:08:21,080 --> 01:08:22,080
(Glancing)

1321
01:08:22,747 --> 01:08:24,414
(Number one is moving to the right.)

1322
01:08:24,414 --> 01:08:26,114
(The opponent has only one blocker!)

1323
01:08:30,347 --> 01:08:32,947
Set by Sol. A quick spike!

1324
01:08:32,947 --> 01:08:35,080
- What a nice play!
- Sol!

1325
01:08:35,547 --> 01:08:39,314
(You did it again!)

1326
01:08:39,814 --> 01:08:43,780
(Fully satisfied)

1327
01:08:43,780 --> 01:08:45,680
Let's make an acrostic poem with her name!

1328
01:08:45,680 --> 01:08:46,747
- Koo!
- Koo Sol!

1329
01:08:46,747 --> 01:08:48,247
- Sol!
- Honestly, you're so good!

1330
01:08:49,347 --> 01:08:50,980
In fact, she joined the court
as a blocker.

1331
01:08:50,980 --> 01:08:53,447
But she just made the most perfect set
of the last three games.

1332
01:08:53,447 --> 01:08:54,347
That's right.

1333
01:08:56,747 --> 01:09:00,647
(Everyone feels proud at this moment.)

1334
01:09:02,780 --> 01:09:05,347
(Sol, the happiest one here)

1335
01:09:05,980 --> 01:09:07,747
(She's playing professional volleyball...)

1336
01:09:07,747 --> 01:09:10,380
(while earning less than 800 dollars
a month.)

1337
01:09:10,791 --> 01:09:12,658
I think I keep playing volleyball
simply because I love it.

1338
01:09:13,791 --> 01:09:17,350
I just really love the moment
I enter the court and touch the ball.

1339
01:09:17,697 --> 01:09:19,252
(Sol's greatest happiness)

1340
01:09:20,160 --> 01:09:21,312
No, let's try blocking once.

1341
01:09:22,229 --> 01:09:24,429
Watch number one.

1342
01:09:24,996 --> 01:09:26,396
Number one!

1343
01:09:26,696 --> 01:09:28,796
(Number one, Hiruma Miharu)

1344
01:09:29,162 --> 01:09:30,662
(Young In's serve)

1345
01:09:31,996 --> 01:09:33,896
- Let's go inside!
- Go inside!

1346
01:09:37,362 --> 01:09:38,329
She's up in the air.

1347
01:09:38,329 --> 01:09:39,929
(Shujitsu High School number one jumps,)

1348
01:09:40,829 --> 01:09:44,829
(and Sol also jumps!)

1349
01:09:44,829 --> 01:09:45,696
Inside.

1350
01:09:46,529 --> 01:09:47,696
Block it.

1351
01:09:47,696 --> 01:09:48,629
That's right!

1352
01:09:48,629 --> 01:09:50,562
(Show us a successful block, Sol!)

1353
01:09:55,129 --> 01:09:56,229
She hit it!

1354
01:09:56,229 --> 01:09:57,824
(She made a mistake while blocking.)

1355
01:09:57,825 --> 01:09:59,996
- Good job.
- I made a mistake.

1356
01:10:00,496 --> 01:10:03,796
(That was so close.)

1357
01:10:03,796 --> 01:10:04,662
That was really close.

1358
01:10:05,096 --> 01:10:06,696
(Oh, my goodness!)

1359
01:10:06,696 --> 01:10:07,829
But,

1360
01:10:07,829 --> 01:10:10,029
- She did a good job.
- it was good.

1361
01:10:10,029 --> 01:10:13,162
- Sol gave 200 percent in her role.
- Yes.

1362
01:10:13,162 --> 01:10:14,929
Now, she's switching with Na Yeon.

1363
01:10:14,929 --> 01:10:16,962
- Okay.
- That was so close!

1364
01:10:16,962 --> 01:10:19,262
(Well done!)

1365
01:10:19,796 --> 01:10:21,581
(Nice job!)

1366
01:10:21,582 --> 01:10:22,496
You did so well.

1367
01:10:23,229 --> 01:10:24,496
Sol, you were so great.

1368
01:10:25,790 --> 01:10:27,987
(Receiving a relay of compliments
from her teammates)

1369
01:10:28,396 --> 01:10:30,062
I almost blocked it, but then it fell.

1370
01:10:31,129 --> 01:10:32,362
Sol actually did...

1371
01:10:33,629 --> 01:10:34,629
a great job on the court.

1372
01:10:35,429 --> 01:10:36,496
She pulled off multiple great plays.

1373
01:10:37,262 --> 01:10:38,129
My heart is aching.

1374
01:10:38,996 --> 01:10:40,562
How was the atmosphere inside?

1375
01:10:40,862 --> 01:10:42,229
It was really good.

1376
01:10:43,329 --> 01:10:46,362
- Two more to go!
- Let's go!

1377
01:10:46,362 --> 01:10:48,362
The Wonder Dogs are leading by two points.

1378
01:10:48,362 --> 01:10:49,529
The score is 22 to 20.

1379
01:10:51,429 --> 01:10:52,496
Toss it high.

1380
01:10:52,496 --> 01:10:53,429
Na Yeon.

1381
01:10:53,429 --> 01:10:54,896
(An accurate set)

1382
01:10:55,662 --> 01:10:56,662
- She jumps.
- Move aside!

1383
01:10:56,662 --> 01:10:58,996
- Great! She scored it.
- She scored.

1384
01:10:58,996 --> 01:11:00,396
It's 20 to 23.

1385
01:11:00,396 --> 01:11:01,396
Hey, Na Yeon.

1386
01:11:07,762 --> 01:11:08,662
Na Yeon.
(She took a sharp leap...)

1387
01:11:09,862 --> 01:11:11,929
(and hammered the ball!)

1388
01:11:12,596 --> 01:11:14,029
- Just one more.
- We just need one more.

1389
01:11:14,029 --> 01:11:15,229
(Second set, Shujitsu High School 21
: Wonder Dogs 24)

1390
01:11:18,729 --> 01:11:22,529
(The atmosphere at Shujitsu High School is
completely down.)

1391
01:11:22,962 --> 01:11:25,096
There you go!

1392
01:11:25,096 --> 01:11:26,362
(Scoring a point is so thrilling!)

1393
01:11:28,029 --> 01:11:29,262
Just one more!

1394
01:11:29,262 --> 01:11:31,796
Wonder Dogs are at set point
in the second set.

1395
01:11:31,796 --> 01:11:34,400
(Go big or go home.)

1396
01:11:37,229 --> 01:11:38,996
(Second set, set point)

1397
01:11:39,662 --> 01:11:41,796
(Hiruma's serve)

1398
01:11:42,362 --> 01:11:43,596
- It's mine!
- She defended.

1399
01:11:44,762 --> 01:11:46,629
- Hye In reaches. She hits it!
- You're doing great right now!

1400
01:11:47,862 --> 01:11:48,896
She covered it at the front.

1401
01:11:48,896 --> 01:11:49,796
Hit it!

1402
01:11:51,029 --> 01:11:53,296
(Setting once again)

1403
01:11:54,029 --> 01:11:55,362
(Toss it to me!)

1404
01:11:59,862 --> 01:12:02,029
(Will she spike it again?)

1405
01:12:02,829 --> 01:12:03,962
- Once again.
- It's mine!

1406
01:12:03,962 --> 01:12:05,696
- She pushes it!
- She did it!

1407
01:12:06,562 --> 01:12:09,096
(This is how Maestro Pyo conducts!)

1408
01:12:10,962 --> 01:12:12,662
- It's 25 to 22!
- Nice.

1409
01:12:12,662 --> 01:12:15,329
The Wonder Dogs take
the second set as well!

1410
01:12:16,729 --> 01:12:17,829
Well done.

1411
01:12:17,829 --> 01:12:19,862
Seung Ju has scored 18 points...

1412
01:12:19,862 --> 01:12:22,062
- in total in both sets.
- Yes.

1413
01:12:23,162 --> 01:12:24,962
(Maestro Pyo played the biggest role
in the second set.)

1414
01:12:24,962 --> 01:12:26,296
Nice job. Well done.

1415
01:12:26,296 --> 01:12:29,129
- That was good. Keep mixing your attacks.
- We're doing great.

1416
01:12:29,129 --> 01:12:32,429
- We have to go all in from the beginning.
- Okay.

1417
01:12:32,929 --> 01:12:35,529
- Let's push them even more at the start.
- Okay.

1418
01:12:35,529 --> 01:12:37,096
We have to do it now.

1419
01:12:38,796 --> 01:12:41,729
Our players are delivering
excellent serves today.

1420
01:12:42,262 --> 01:12:43,196
They're all doing great.
They're well-focused.

1421
01:12:44,196 --> 01:12:45,629
The problem is whether it stays.

1422
01:12:45,629 --> 01:12:46,629
We have just one more set to go.

1423
01:12:47,996 --> 01:12:50,462
(Meanwhile,
Shujitsu High School's time-out)

1424
01:12:51,762 --> 01:12:53,296
Are your brains even working right now?

1425
01:12:57,362 --> 01:12:59,296
You're not doing what you should be doing.

1426
01:12:59,296 --> 01:13:01,496
The setter keeps playing
with the same pattern.

1427
01:13:01,496 --> 01:13:02,896
That's why they've got
two blockers marking you.

1428
01:13:06,629 --> 01:13:08,762
Being impatient won't help you score.

1429
01:13:09,762 --> 01:13:11,796
The center player is really tall.

1430
01:13:11,796 --> 01:13:15,196
So, their weakness is on the wings.

1431
01:13:16,096 --> 01:13:18,484
(Switching attack route
from the middle to the sides)

1432
01:13:20,162 --> 01:13:21,328
Alright. Stay focused.

1433
01:13:24,328 --> 01:13:27,628
- Let's go and win this!
- Let's go!

1434
01:13:30,063 --> 01:13:33,896
(Team Japan is on the brink.)

1435
01:13:35,108 --> 01:13:36,308
Fight until the end!

1436
01:13:36,975 --> 01:13:40,075
If Wonder Dogs win this set,
it's their victory.

1437
01:13:41,741 --> 01:13:43,141
Let's go, guys!

1438
01:13:43,141 --> 01:13:44,575
(We're finishing it with this set.)

1439
01:13:45,741 --> 01:13:48,341
(Third set, Shujitsu High School 0
: Wonder Dogs 0)

1440
01:13:49,041 --> 01:13:50,341
Young In.

1441
01:13:54,975 --> 01:13:57,175
Kato Uta from Shujitsu serves,

1442
01:13:57,175 --> 01:13:58,475
and the third set begins.

1443
01:14:02,408 --> 01:14:04,641
(A perfect one-block spot)

1444
01:14:07,075 --> 01:14:08,841
They try to block it but fail.

1445
01:14:08,841 --> 01:14:11,975
That was a wonderful play.

1446
01:14:13,041 --> 01:14:17,975
(Taking the early lead)

1447
01:14:18,708 --> 01:14:21,241
(The one-block tactic is working perfectly
from the start.)

1448
01:14:25,608 --> 01:14:26,641
Yoshimoto serves.

1449
01:14:31,308 --> 01:14:32,808
That was shaky.

1450
01:14:34,708 --> 01:14:35,608
Fast center push.

1451
01:14:36,475 --> 01:14:37,441
They save it.

1452
01:14:37,808 --> 01:14:41,308
(Shujitsu's free ball)

1453
01:14:41,808 --> 01:14:43,741
(Assembling the iron wall)

1454
01:14:49,775 --> 01:14:52,275
Spike, and it's blocked!
Point for the Wonder Dogs.

1455
01:14:52,275 --> 01:14:53,641
That was a nice block.

1456
01:14:53,641 --> 01:14:55,008
- Nice.
- Nice.

1457
01:14:55,975 --> 01:14:57,841
They've practically built a wall.

1458
01:14:57,841 --> 01:14:59,008
Yes, that was Myoung Hwa.

1459
01:14:59,008 --> 01:15:01,608
(Third set, Shujitsu High School 1
: Wonder Dogs 2)

1460
01:15:02,741 --> 01:15:05,808
(Hiruma Miharu serving)

1461
01:15:08,508 --> 01:15:09,608
The reception was shaky.

1462
01:15:09,755 --> 01:15:11,441
(A shaky toss)

1463
01:15:11,641 --> 01:15:12,808
(Chae Rim spikes)

1464
01:15:13,975 --> 01:15:14,841
Chae Rim!

1465
01:15:15,208 --> 01:15:16,008
They save it.

1466
01:15:16,408 --> 01:15:18,508
(Shujitsu's chance to attack)

1467
01:15:18,508 --> 01:15:20,741
To the side! Watch the sides!

1468
01:15:22,121 --> 01:15:24,154
(The attack line spreads to the sides)

1469
01:15:24,621 --> 01:15:27,388
(Where will they attack from?)

1470
01:15:30,654 --> 01:15:31,754
Spike from the right!

1471
01:15:32,988 --> 01:15:33,988
(Touches)

1472
01:15:36,542 --> 01:15:38,223
(Block touch out)

1473
01:15:38,224 --> 01:15:39,924
Sorry, that was my miss.

1474
01:15:46,146 --> 01:15:48,146
(Shujitsu confused the blockers,)

1475
01:15:48,780 --> 01:15:51,480
(and attacked from the side
in an instant.)

1476
01:15:51,813 --> 01:15:53,946
(They tried to block,
but it was too late.)

1477
01:15:57,013 --> 01:15:59,913
(The side attack tactic is
very effective.)

1478
01:16:01,280 --> 01:16:03,480
Shujitsu High is leading by one point.

1479
01:16:06,313 --> 01:16:07,413
(Shaky reception)

1480
01:16:07,413 --> 01:16:08,413
It hits the net,
and they save it well.

1481
01:16:11,846 --> 01:16:12,713
(Barely pushed it over)

1482
01:16:12,713 --> 01:16:13,746
The ball is in the middle.

1483
01:16:13,746 --> 01:16:14,746
They toss it.

1484
01:16:16,780 --> 01:16:19,080
(The attackers are scattered again!)

1485
01:16:19,780 --> 01:16:22,380
(Where will it come from this time?)

1486
01:16:23,380 --> 01:16:24,380
They toss it to the other side.

1487
01:16:24,880 --> 01:16:26,513
(Spike from the right again)

1488
01:16:26,813 --> 01:16:27,813
They push it over,

1489
01:16:28,813 --> 01:16:29,980
but they save it and toss it up.

1490
01:16:31,146 --> 01:16:32,480
(It's the Wonder Dogs' attack)

1491
01:16:32,580 --> 01:16:34,080
Make it long.

1492
01:16:40,013 --> 01:16:41,046
She used her fist.

1493
01:16:41,480 --> 01:16:42,446
Come on, Chae Rim!

1494
01:16:43,846 --> 01:16:44,846
They made the pass.

1495
01:16:47,280 --> 01:16:48,213
Spike!

1496
01:16:50,046 --> 01:16:51,780
A diving save!

1497
01:16:53,280 --> 01:16:54,846
(Wonder Dogs' second chance)

1498
01:16:57,580 --> 01:16:58,546
They push it over.

1499
01:16:58,546 --> 01:16:59,680
Get ready to attack!

1500
01:17:01,146 --> 01:17:02,046
They toss it, and...

1501
01:17:02,313 --> 01:17:03,146
spike from the middle.

1502
01:17:03,146 --> 01:17:04,280
(Attacks pushing in)

1503
01:17:05,680 --> 01:17:06,880
- Successful defense!
- She blocks it!

1504
01:17:09,713 --> 01:17:10,713
Jumping up.

1505
01:17:10,713 --> 01:17:11,746
(Powerful spike)

1506
01:17:12,546 --> 01:17:13,613
Diagonal attack.

1507
01:17:14,480 --> 01:17:15,313
They set it up.

1508
01:17:15,313 --> 01:17:17,346
It's coming. It's our free ball.

1509
01:17:17,346 --> 01:17:19,313
(All rushing)

1510
01:17:22,846 --> 01:17:24,046
They block it.

1511
01:17:25,380 --> 01:17:26,380
Our free ball.

1512
01:17:32,513 --> 01:17:33,546
Spike!

1513
01:17:37,580 --> 01:17:38,746
It's blocked.

1514
01:17:40,313 --> 01:17:43,513
(The early momentum shifts in an instant.)

1515
01:17:44,446 --> 01:17:47,446
(On fire)

1516
01:17:49,913 --> 01:17:51,546
(Riding on the momentum)

1517
01:17:51,546 --> 01:17:52,513
Back toss.

1518
01:17:52,713 --> 01:17:53,813
Spike!

1519
01:17:53,813 --> 01:17:56,413
(Every spike turns into a point.)

1520
01:17:57,613 --> 01:17:59,646
(Third set, Shujitsu High School 7
: Wonder Dogs 5)

1521
01:18:02,613 --> 01:18:04,813
(They keep working the sides.)

1522
01:18:04,813 --> 01:18:06,746
It hits the net and falls.

1523
01:18:07,480 --> 01:18:08,380
Sorry.

1524
01:18:09,380 --> 01:18:11,246
(Shujitsu are on fire.)

1525
01:18:11,246 --> 01:18:12,380
Attack to the middle back.

1526
01:18:12,613 --> 01:18:13,680
(Powerful pipe attack)

1527
01:18:13,680 --> 01:18:15,313
The ball is out.

1528
01:18:15,313 --> 01:18:18,380
Shujitsu have completely taken
control of the game!

1529
01:18:18,380 --> 01:18:20,646
(Third set, Shujitsu High School 10
: Wonder Dogs 8)

1530
01:18:23,246 --> 01:18:24,613
The score is now 8 to 10.

1531
01:18:25,780 --> 01:18:28,113
(Na Yeon serving)

1532
01:18:28,113 --> 01:18:29,146
Na Yeon serves.

1533
01:18:30,313 --> 01:18:31,846
Watch out for player number one!

1534
01:18:32,413 --> 01:18:33,780
Player number one!

1535
01:18:33,780 --> 01:18:35,813
Watch out for player number three!

1536
01:18:37,646 --> 01:18:39,080
Focus on player number six.

1537
01:18:41,680 --> 01:18:44,780
(Coach Yeon Koung is the only one
watching number six.)

1538
01:18:48,380 --> 01:18:50,680
(A stable reception)

1539
01:18:51,846 --> 01:18:54,680
(All moving in perfect coordination)

1540
01:18:54,880 --> 01:18:56,946
Number one is moving around!

1541
01:18:56,946 --> 01:18:58,013
Move back!

1542
01:19:00,580 --> 01:19:01,980
Where will they aim this time?

1543
01:19:04,546 --> 01:19:06,680
(We got you, number six!)

1544
01:19:06,680 --> 01:19:09,213
To the left, and blocked!

1545
01:19:09,213 --> 01:19:11,280
- A successful block!
- Nice block!

1546
01:19:17,246 --> 01:19:20,713
(This is a perfectly read block.)

1547
01:19:22,080 --> 01:19:23,946
(So proud)

1548
01:19:24,380 --> 01:19:27,080
(The chase begins now.)

1549
01:19:27,280 --> 01:19:28,180
Let's not make this hard.

1550
01:19:28,180 --> 01:19:29,480
Just one more.

1551
01:19:29,480 --> 01:19:31,280
Good job, Young In.

1552
01:19:33,146 --> 01:19:35,380
The gap is still two points.

1553
01:19:37,546 --> 01:19:41,113
(The setter is the key to a good attack.)

1554
01:19:42,180 --> 01:19:46,313
If the setters do their job well,
they won't be able to single block, right?

1555
01:19:46,980 --> 01:19:47,880
Number nine looks low.

1556
01:19:50,046 --> 01:19:52,380
(Aiming for player nine to single block)

1557
01:19:54,013 --> 01:19:55,480
Spike to the center!

1558
01:19:55,480 --> 01:19:56,446
- Yes.
- Great.

1559
01:19:57,880 --> 01:19:59,846
- Nice toss.
- Nice.

1560
01:20:01,346 --> 01:20:02,780
It was a good toss,

1561
