Coach Yeon Koung talked about)

1618
01:22:23,080 --> 01:22:26,413
(Nice straight shot)

1619
01:22:27,280 --> 01:22:28,680
Get to the line!

1620
01:22:29,846 --> 01:22:32,446
(Senba Kokoro throws herself to dig.)

1621
01:22:35,913 --> 01:22:38,513
(But she failed.)

1622
01:22:39,446 --> 01:22:40,746
- Chae Rim!
- Nice!

1623
01:22:40,746 --> 01:22:41,813
Block out!

1624
01:22:41,813 --> 01:22:47,013
Chae Rim is taking every chance
to hit off the block today.

1625
01:22:48,146 --> 01:22:50,746
- Nice toss. Seriously.
- Nice.

1626
01:22:50,746 --> 01:22:52,013
Nice, Chae Rim!

1627
01:22:52,334 --> 01:22:54,667
If a tactic works,
keep doing it until it doesn't.

1628
01:22:54,667 --> 01:22:55,420
Of course!

1629
01:22:55,767 --> 01:22:57,801
The Wonder Dogs tie again.

1630
01:22:57,801 --> 01:22:58,867
It's 11 to 11.

1631
01:22:59,367 --> 01:23:00,267
Na Yeon!

1632
01:23:00,901 --> 01:23:03,334
It's okay to give it to her again.

1633
01:23:03,334 --> 01:23:04,901
It's fine to set her again.

1634
01:23:04,901 --> 01:23:06,634
Have faith in Young In.

1635
01:23:07,034 --> 01:23:07,901
Young In!
Watch player number nine.

1636
01:23:08,901 --> 01:23:11,467
(Specific instructions on who to defend)

1637
01:23:11,467 --> 01:23:12,901
Watch out for number nine.

1638
01:23:17,329 --> 01:23:18,429
(Crashing)

1639
01:23:19,082 --> 01:23:21,515
(Paths tangling)

1640
01:23:26,862 --> 01:23:29,195
