in the front row.)

1806
01:33:16,360 --> 01:33:19,060
(With the front setter gone,
another setter will be at the back.)

1807
01:33:21,379 --> 01:33:24,813
(The team now has three strikers
at the front.)

1808
01:33:24,813 --> 01:33:25,813
Coach.

1809
01:33:26,179 --> 01:33:27,479
- Do we go with two?
- Yeah. Two players.

1810
01:33:27,979 --> 01:33:29,846
- Enkhsoyol, do it confidently.
- Yes, Coach.

1811
01:33:33,246 --> 01:33:34,346
(They substitute Young In with Lee Jin.)

1812
01:33:34,346 --> 01:33:35,613
Na Yeon, switch with Enkhsoyol.

1813
01:33:36,646 --> 01:33:39,379
Let's go.

1814
01:33:40,879 --> 01:33:42,446
Come here, Enkhsoyol.

1815
01:33:42,446 --> 01:33:43,646
Yes.

1816
01:33:44,746 --> 01:33:46,646
It's a strategy to substitute two players,

1817
01:33:46,646 --> 01:33:50,379
so that there are three attackers
in the front row.

1818
01:33:50,513 --> 01:33:53,413
Enkhsoyol seemed to be doing fine
during training.

1819
01:33:53,413 --> 01:33:57,113
We substituted players
to increase the success rate in attacks.

1820
01:33:57,546 --> 01:33:59,213
It's 16 to 16.

1821
01:34:00,679 --> 01:34:02,913
Enkhsoyol, mark number three.

1822
01:34:02,913 --> 01:34:04,513
Look where number three goes.

1823
01:34:04,513 --> 01:34:05,546
Yes.

1824
01:34:05,546 --> 01:34:07,279
(With number three again)

1825
01:34:07,879 --> 01:34:08,879
Serve!

1826
01:34:08,879 --> 01:34:11,046
(Lee Jin serves.)

1827
01:34:12,679 --> 01:34:14,079
That was a nice serve.

1828
01:34:14,079 --> 01:34:15,079
(It shook their reception.)

1829
01:34:15,846 --> 01:34:17,813
It's a spike, but they defended it.
Lee Jin!

1830
01:34:18,579 --> 01:34:20,113
The ball is in the air, and she spikes!

1831
01:34:20,113 --> 01:34:21,113
(Baek Chae Rim's spike)

1832
01:34:27,046 --> 01:34:28,046
Get it!

1833
01:34:40,979 --> 01:34:41,979
It hurts.

1834
01:34:43,946 --> 01:34:47,946
(Baek Chae Rim collapses.)

1835
01:34:48,413 --> 01:34:49,446
That shook me.

1836
01:34:51,646 --> 01:34:53,679
(Rushing in an emergency)

1837
01:34:54,946 --> 01:34:57,379
She suddenly fell on her ankle.

1838
01:34:57,379 --> 01:35:00,646
(The hitter at the front clutches
her ankle.)

1839
01:35:05,779 --> 01:35:07,546
(A little earlier)

1840
01:35:14,113 --> 01:35:17,513
(She twisted her ankle on the landing.)

1841
01:35:20,113 --> 01:35:21,146
How did she fall?

1842
01:35:23,079 --> 01:35:24,079
It hurts.

1843
01:35:25,546 --> 01:35:27,546
I wanted to win.

1844
01:35:28,179 --> 01:35:29,446
Hit it!

1845
01:35:29,713 --> 01:35:34,213
(Chae Rim kept spiking hard
throughout the previous sets.)

1846
01:35:35,513 --> 01:35:38,846
I thought I had to do great.

1847
01:35:41,479 --> 01:35:43,479
(She gradually slumps down.)

1848
01:35:43,479 --> 01:35:45,379
So I put in more strength.

1849
01:35:46,446 --> 01:35:48,646
(She ran out of energy in the end.)

1850
01:35:48,646 --> 01:35:51,613
She attacked several times,
so she may be exhausted now.

1851
01:35:54,379 --> 01:35:55,946
I guess I got ahead of myself.

1852
01:35:58,579 --> 01:36:03,246
(Chae Rim collapses
after hitting the ball.)

1853
01:36:03,613 --> 01:36:04,913
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine.

1854
01:36:05,146 --> 01:36:06,179
- Are you all right?
- Yeah.

1855
01:36:07,013 --> 01:36:08,113
Did it twist?

1856
01:36:08,113 --> 01:36:09,113
It's fine.

1857
01:36:09,946 --> 01:36:11,146
- You're okay, right?
- I am.

1858
01:36:12,346 --> 01:36:13,846
- Are you okay?
- I'm great.

1859
01:36:15,613 --> 01:36:16,746
Are you all right, Chae Rim?

1860
01:36:16,746 --> 01:36:18,546
Yes. I'm fine.

1861
01:36:19,846 --> 01:36:20,879
- Okay?
- No play?

1862
01:36:21,179 --> 01:36:22,646
No play. Serve!

1863
01:36:23,146 --> 01:36:24,446
- Okay?
- No play?

1864
01:36:25,179 --> 01:36:26,513
So far,

1865
01:36:27,546 --> 01:36:30,546
it's great to hear
that there's no problem.

1866
01:36:30,546 --> 01:36:32,879
It will be a replay in this case.

1867
01:36:32,879 --> 01:36:34,746
They won't count the previous rally...

1868
01:36:34,746 --> 01:36:35,979
- and will start over.
- You're right.

1869
01:36:35,979 --> 01:36:37,479
No play. Serve!

1870
01:36:38,179 --> 01:36:41,713
(Lee Jin prepares to serve again.)

1871
01:36:46,779 --> 01:36:49,613
No replay. You touched it,
so it's an error.

1872
01:36:50,513 --> 01:36:52,446
No replay. You touched it,
so it's an error.

1873
01:36:54,379 --> 01:36:55,479
It's a fault. You touched it.

1874
01:36:56,846 --> 01:36:58,713
No!

1875
01:36:58,713 --> 01:37:00,046
Why suddenly switch from a no play?

1876
01:37:00,979 --> 01:37:03,446
(The Wonder Dogs' net touch error)

1877
01:37:03,446 --> 01:37:06,946
- That's not true!
- No. It was a no play!

1878
01:37:06,946 --> 01:37:09,046
We're going back to the...

1879
01:37:09,879 --> 01:37:10,879
It's a net touch?

1880
01:37:11,379 --> 01:37:12,946
- What?
- What's going on?

1881
01:37:15,179 --> 01:37:16,946
- No!
- It's not!

1882
01:37:16,946 --> 01:37:18,246
Why suddenly change from a no play?

1883
01:37:20,413 --> 01:37:21,579
No!

1884
01:37:25,313 --> 01:37:28,813
The first signal was a no play.
Why would he suddenly change it?

1885
01:37:28,846 --> 01:37:31,246
(The score of 16 to 16 is
a crucial point.)

1886
01:37:31,246 --> 01:37:33,579
No replay. The net is touched.

1887
01:37:38,013 --> 01:37:39,046
No replay.

1888
01:37:42,313 --> 01:37:46,213
We thought the game was stopped
because Chae Rim fell.

1889
01:37:47,313 --> 01:37:51,179
The referee states it's a net touch,
not a replay.

1890
01:37:52,046 --> 01:37:54,613
(Shujitsu High School 17 : Wonder Dogs 16)

1891
01:37:55,446 --> 01:37:59,513
(They gave one point in the first set.)

1892
01:38:00,213 --> 01:38:03,946
(And they gave another just now.)

1893
01:38:06,879 --> 01:38:08,579
Come out.

1894
01:38:10,846 --> 01:38:11,979
Come out.

1895
01:38:11,979 --> 01:38:13,513
(Boldly telling them to come over)

1896
01:38:14,413 --> 01:38:19,379
(Is the team just leaving the court?)

1897
01:38:20,179 --> 01:38:22,813
(The game stopped?)

1898
01:38:23,446 --> 01:38:25,913
(Thinking for a moment
after the referee's decision)

1899
01:38:26,679 --> 01:38:28,579
Come out.

1900
01:38:29,146 --> 01:38:30,846
(Come out so we can switch the libero.)

1901
01:38:30,846 --> 01:38:32,579
You can start now!

1902
01:38:33,146 --> 01:38:34,213
No replay.

1903
01:38:34,213 --> 01:38:35,313
One more point.

1904
01:38:38,546 --> 01:38:40,246
Enkhsoyol. Chae Rim.

1905
01:38:40,246 --> 01:38:41,279
(As if it's nothing)

1906
01:38:41,579 --> 01:38:43,579
It's okay. Don't be shaken!

1907
01:38:43,579 --> 01:38:45,346
We can turn this around!

1908
01:38:45,346 --> 01:38:46,513
It's 16 to 17.

1909
01:38:49,846 --> 01:38:54,279
It's frustrating.
That was an irritating situation.

1910
01:38:55,779 --> 01:38:58,213
But it's part of the game.

1911
01:38:59,146 --> 01:39:00,146
Well...

1912
01:39:00,846 --> 01:39:02,179
it's done by people.

1913
01:39:02,179 --> 01:39:04,546
So there can be mistakes.

1914
01:39:04,946 --> 01:39:06,646
It's part of the game.

1915
01:39:07,146 --> 01:39:09,646
It can happen when we play.

1916
01:39:10,246 --> 01:39:14,446
Whatever the result is,
I think it's part of the sports.

1917
01:39:14,646 --> 01:39:16,646
More than that,
we need to win the third set.

1918
01:39:17,546 --> 01:39:19,113
What's more important for me was...

1919
01:39:19,479 --> 01:39:21,213
our performance during the match.

1920
01:39:21,546 --> 01:39:23,379
One more point for a tie!

1921
01:39:24,213 --> 01:39:26,713
(The Wonder Dogs stay composed.)

1922
01:39:26,713 --> 01:39:28,413
Catch the ball first!

1923
01:39:30,185 --> 01:39:31,185
Enkhsoyol!

1924
01:39:31,186 --> 01:39:32,591
- I told you not to go there.
- Yes, Coach.

1925
01:39:32,592 --> 01:39:33,818
- Come here.
- Yes.

1926
01:39:33,819 --> 01:39:35,879
(Explaining her weakness
in the previous rally)

1927
01:39:39,879 --> 01:39:40,979
Where are you going?

1928
01:39:42,352 --> 01:39:44,619
- Enkhsoyol, don't hold back.
- Okay.

1929
01:39:46,479 --> 01:39:48,646
We can turn this back!

1930
01:39:48,646 --> 01:39:50,961
(We must get a point back.)

1931
01:39:51,846 --> 01:39:53,446
We can turn this back!

1932
01:39:54,713 --> 01:39:55,979
The side block is low.

1933
01:39:56,213 --> 01:39:57,913
Their left block is not high.

1934
01:39:58,146 --> 01:39:59,179
Understood!

1935
01:39:59,479 --> 01:40:01,713
Watch the one who serves!

1936
01:40:01,713 --> 01:40:03,479
(Uchida Riona serves.)

1937
01:40:03,479 --> 01:40:04,813
Mine!

1938
01:40:05,346 --> 01:40:07,513
(She tosses carefully to the left.)

1939
01:40:09,013 --> 01:40:11,746
(Enkhsoyol jumps.)

1940
01:40:12,379 --> 01:40:13,846
How should you hit when the block is low?

1941
01:40:13,846 --> 01:40:16,713
There's a straight line in front of you.
Aim there and hit it.

1942
01:40:16,713 --> 01:40:19,546
(She should hit straight to the line
when the block is low.)

1943
01:40:20,579 --> 01:40:22,779
(I'm watching you, Yes Girl.)

1944
01:40:23,146 --> 01:40:26,013
I'm Enkhsoyol from Mongolia.

1945
01:40:27,579 --> 01:40:28,713
Enkhsoyol!

1946
01:40:28,713 --> 01:40:33,379
(Yeon Koung had a soft spot
for Enkhsoyol.)

1947
01:40:34,093 --> 01:40:36,813
(Due to a communication issue,)

1948
01:40:37,613 --> 01:40:41,413
(Coach Kim kept a close eye on her
out of concern.)

1949
01:40:41,546 --> 01:40:42,546
Yes!

1950
01:40:42,546 --> 01:40:44,179
(She answers well at least.)

1951
01:40:45,479 --> 01:40:49,379
(Did you understand the strategy
to hit straight?)

1952
01:40:49,379 --> 01:40:52,013
Hit it, Enkhsoyol!

1953
01:40:52,613 --> 01:40:53,713
Hit it, Enkhsoyol!

1954
01:40:53,713 --> 01:40:55,546
(The red arrow is
where Enkhsoyol's ball goes.)

1955
01:40:55,546 --> 01:40:57,413
(The green arrow is
the direction she should attack.)

1956
01:40:57,413 --> 01:40:58,679
Hit it!

1957
01:40:58,679 --> 01:41:00,946
(Wrong direction)

1958
01:41:01,546 --> 01:41:03,179
(Again?)

1959
01:41:03,513 --> 01:41:05,813
It's a back C. Number 3!

1960
01:41:05,813 --> 01:41:07,146
(Enkhsoyol's mistake is...)

1961
01:41:12,579 --> 01:41:14,479
(followed by losing a point.)

1962
01:41:14,479 --> 01:41:15,513
Enkhsoyol!

1963
01:41:15,679 --> 01:41:16,879
Where should you hit?

1964
01:41:18,546 --> 01:41:19,679
Enkhsoyol!

1965
01:41:19,679 --> 01:41:20,979
Where should you hit?

1966
01:41:21,513 --> 01:41:22,779
Where should you hit?

1967
01:41:23,746 --> 01:41:24,846
Go for a long shot.

1968
01:41:26,179 --> 01:41:27,513
(She needs to overcome her nerves.)

1969
01:41:27,513 --> 01:41:31,313
I think getting nervous was
also a problem for me.

1970
01:41:32,413 --> 01:41:36,379
(Shujitsu High School 19 : Wonder Dogs 16)

1971
01:41:40,213 --> 01:41:42,713
The serve is fast. Stay back!

1972
01:41:43,246 --> 01:41:45,313
(Bring it on!)

1973
01:41:48,113 --> 01:41:50,013
- Mine.
- Send it up!

1974
01:41:50,013 --> 01:41:51,846
(The reception was a little shaky.)

1975
01:41:51,846 --> 01:41:53,679
Lee Jin uses an underhand pass.

1976
01:41:55,879 --> 01:41:56,913
Spike!

1977
01:41:57,613 --> 01:41:58,946
They defended it.

1978
01:42:01,482 --> 01:42:03,949
(Tossing quickly to number 3)

1979
01:42:07,054 --> 01:42:08,421
A spike to the right!

1980
01:42:08,921 --> 01:42:10,621
They score with a block out.

1981
01:42:11,521 --> 01:42:13,988
- We need to get the flow back!
- Let's do this!

1982
01:42:14,829 --> 01:42:18,262
(They can't seem to score.)

1983
01:42:19,388 --> 01:42:22,855
(Meanwhile, Shujitsu High School gets
their momentum.)

1984
01:42:23,396 --> 01:42:25,462
(They easily get a point with a spike.)

1985
01:42:25,462 --> 01:42:27,429
It's empty in between. Come forward!

1986
01:42:29,162 --> 01:42:31,896
- She jumps, and it's a tip.
- They should have watched that.

1987
01:42:31,896 --> 01:42:34,129
(They even tipped it wisely.)

1988
01:42:34,129 --> 01:42:36,562
(The atmosphere is...)

1989
01:42:36,562 --> 01:42:39,062
(getting more intense.)

1990
01:42:39,429 --> 01:42:41,329
(Hooray!)

1991
01:42:41,329 --> 01:42:45,762
Shujitsu High School is on fire right now.

1992
01:42:46,562 --> 01:42:49,996
(Shujitsu High School 21 : Wonder Dogs 18)

1993
01:42:50,714 --> 01:42:52,514
(We should change the momentum.)

1994
01:42:52,562 --> 01:42:54,762
It made me think carefully.

1995
01:42:55,696 --> 01:42:59,429
What I expect from Enkhsoyol is scoring
with her attacks.

1996
01:43:00,462 --> 01:43:05,562
I thought she acted differently
from what I wanted her to do.

1997
01:43:05,562 --> 01:43:09,129
How should I help
my players improve once more?

1998
01:43:09,130 --> 01:43:10,448
(But the head coach must
also use such players.)

1999
01:43:12,329 --> 01:43:13,429
Enkhsoyol!

2000
01:43:13,429 --> 01:43:15,229
There's number six.

2001
01:43:16,162 --> 01:43:18,463
(Glancing)

2002
01:43:21,695 --> 01:43:23,435
Focus on scoring three points.

2003
01:43:24,839 --> 01:43:27,341
(It's Hyeon Jeong's turn to serve.)

2004
01:43:34,215 --> 01:43:37,185
(The attack is coming from both wings
again.)

2005
01:43:37,578 --> 01:43:40,648
(Where will the setter place the ball?)

2006
01:43:42,683 --> 01:43:44,270
(As predicted, she tosses
the ball toward number six.)

2007
01:43:44,271 --> 01:43:45,271
She'll hit it!

2008
01:43:46,020 --> 01:43:51,425
(They deceived both Seung Ju
and Myoung Hwa.)

2009
01:43:51,992 --> 01:43:56,029
(There's only Enkhsoyol to block
the attack.)

2010
01:43:56,301 --> 01:43:57,301
(Enkhsoyol,)

2011
01:43:58,835 --> 01:44:00,401
(remember how I said
number six would spike?)

2012
01:44:06,178 --> 01:44:07,178
A spike.

2013
01:44:07,179 --> 01:44:08,842
(Did she manage to block it?)

2014
01:44:09,810 --> 01:44:11,879
(Shujitsu High School's libero rushes
toward the ball.)

2015
01:44:12,346 --> 01:44:15,749
You can get it!

2016
01:44:21,520 --> 01:44:25,759
- Will it get blocked?
- Now, there you go!

2017
01:44:25,964 --> 01:44:27,297
Enkhsoyol!

2018
01:44:29,263 --> 01:44:31,765
(Coach, I did it!)

2019
01:44:31,766 --> 01:44:34,201
Enkhsoyol!

2020
01:44:34,709 --> 01:44:38,461
Enkhsoyol fully crouched
and jumped high...

2021
01:44:38,615 --> 01:44:41,175
- to solely block that one attack!
- That's right.

2022
01:44:41,335 --> 01:44:45,707
I hope this point will help Enkhsoyol feel
more confident.

2023
01:44:45,708 --> 01:44:47,314
(Third set, Shujitsu High School 21
: Wonder Dogs 19)

2024
01:44:47,554 --> 01:44:49,606
Myoung Hwa, mark number three first.

2025
01:44:50,049 --> 01:44:54,153
(With foresight, Coach assigns a mark
once again.)

2026
01:44:55,189 --> 01:44:58,092
(Hyeon Jeong's second serve)

2027
01:44:58,429 --> 01:44:59,526
Hyeon Jeong serves.

2028
01:44:59,527 --> 01:45:01,662
(A shaky reception)

2029
01:45:02,196 --> 01:45:02,930
What?

2030
01:45:04,632 --> 01:45:06,934
(Who will attack this time?)

2031
01:45:07,484 --> 01:45:09,511
(Myoung Hwa, mark number three first.)

2032
01:45:10,871 --> 01:45:13,741
(You haven't forgotten what I said,
have you?)

2033
01:45:14,962 --> 01:45:15,962
A back toss.

2034
01:45:17,170 --> 01:45:18,876
It's number three!

2035
01:45:19,847 --> 01:45:22,383
(As the coach said,
the ball is delivered to number three!)

2036
01:45:24,035 --> 01:45:25,052
- A spike.
- Nice!

2037
01:45:29,215 --> 01:45:32,926
It's blocked!

2038
01:45:32,991 --> 01:45:34,895
They're catching up again!
Now, they're just one point behind!

2039
01:45:35,663 --> 01:45:41,502
(The impenetrable wall is back.)

2040
01:45:42,002 --> 01:45:44,064
(Everything goes
as the Wonder Coach plans.)

2041
01:45:44,065 --> 01:45:45,339
That block was so good just now.

2042
01:45:45,375 --> 01:45:46,855
As far as I remember,

2043
01:45:46,874 --> 01:45:49,243
I'm sure it was in the first set,
in the same exact situation,

2044
01:45:49,789 --> 01:45:53,388
Shujitsu High School players have made
the same mistake.

2045
01:45:53,721 --> 01:45:57,407
- This could lead to great opportunities.
- That's right.

2046
01:45:57,760 --> 01:45:59,987
The score is 20 to 21
with just a one-point gap!

2047
01:46:02,956 --> 01:46:05,088
(To break through the strongest
Japanese high school team,)

2048
01:46:05,379 --> 01:46:06,772
(the underdogs persistently give it
their all.)

2049
01:46:07,459 --> 01:46:10,862
(How will
this desperate international match end?)

2050
01:46:11,024 --> 01:46:13,024
(Their fourth opponent is
Kwangju Women's University.)

2051
01:46:13,171 --> 01:46:16,157
(They won every award in the league.)

2052
01:46:16,643 --> 01:46:17,757
I started to get worried.

2053
01:46:18,439 --> 01:46:20,146
I'll solve all your problems.

2054
01:46:20,205 --> 01:46:21,607
- So, just focus on playing boldly.
- Yes, sir!

2055
01:46:21,620 --> 01:46:22,620
Serve to number two.

2056
01:46:24,010 --> 01:46:24,944
(His prediction hits the mark.)

2057
01:46:25,951 --> 01:46:28,890
Keep going! Stop the ball! Feint! Aim
at the target, and hit it with confidence!

2058
01:46:28,891 --> 01:46:30,349
(Amid all the intense strategies,)

2059
01:46:31,040 --> 01:46:32,585
(will the Wonder Coach find
a breakthrough?)
